{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/11947-1001-mage-story-hooks","id":11947,"title":"1001 Mage Story Hooks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-16T01:15:11-08:00","id":11947,"title":"1001 Mage Story Hooks","content":"Reposting my old 1001 Mage Story Hooks thread here, because that sort of thread tends to be useful.<br /> <br /> Please be aware that the numbers won't be consecutive - I created this thread on three separate fora.<br /> <br /> 1) Something terrible happened, and the soul of the PC's husband is in danger of simply fading away. Perhaps some mage highly knowledgeable on the topic of souls might help? Like, say, a Tremere or any other Reaper?<br /> <br /> 2) Through some clever acts of terrorism (taking the loved ones of a couple powerful mages hostage, etc.), and with the tacit support of the Free Council, one of the Nameless Orders manages to take over an entire city.<br /> <br /> Now the Lex Magica is a thing of the past, and mages get to do anything - anything - they want with and to whomever they want.<br /> <br /> 3) A powerful Adamantine Arrow has recently gone Vidantus - she left the order, claiming that she couldn't bear the violence and bloodshed of the Adamantine Way any more.<br /> <br /> Terrible timing, with the consilium under attack by vicious packs of werewolves and their spirit allies.<br /> <br /> The Adamantine Arrow needs her back, by any means possible.<br /> <br /> 4) One of the most skilled Acanthus prophets has seen the PC's imminent death in her dreams.<br /> <br /> 5) The PCs get to see what they believe to be real, unmistakable proof of the Exarch's existence and their power and influence.<br /> <br /> How does this influence their religious and political views?<br /> <br /> 6) By some bizarre twist of fate, one of the PC's Sleeper friends gets to know the real names of all members of a particularly paranoid Panopticon pylon.<br /> <br /> After the Sleeper has survived one attempt on his life, committed by some servants of the pylon - under the influence of a powerful Profane Urim - , he approaches the PCs, asking for help.<br /> <br /> 7) During an occult investigation, the PCs meet a woman whose mind and soul show strange signs of influence and tampering, most likely by Mind magic. Very little of the young woman's original personality is left.<br /> <br /> Who edited her mind, and for what purpose? Can her original personality be regained?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 8) The cabal somehow comes into the possession of a unique and powerful artifact. After a little bit of research they learn that it might be The Key which could free a now fallen supernal entity imprisoned somewhere in the Fallen World. There are conflicting accounts as to the nature of the entity. By some accounts it is a benevolent being that would be inclined to grant great boons to those who free it, while other tales claim that it was a mad and wrathful tyrant that once freed would vent its rage by inflicting an untold level of devastation upon the world as it lashes out against the Exarchs' servants.<br /> <br /> The PC's have to determine whether they wish to free the fallen god or not while guarding against attempts by the Seers and rival cabals who will attempt to take The Key from them to either free the entity for his boons or to keep it locked up indefinitely.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And of course if the PC's do decide to free the entity they'll have to first discover the location of its prison and then make the surely perilous quest to get there while all the while fending off seers and other adversaries.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 9) One of the larger cabals have been tying their symbols more and more to Esoteric Nazism, and their ranks have been swelling with new Mages in unprecedented numbers. Their leader claims they can help Sleepers on the path to Awakening, and all evidence points to the claim being possibly true...<br /> <br /> 10) A small Free Council/Mysterium cabal have been opened up a new fast food restaurant to see what happens when you mix Prime magic with food and give it to Sleepers...<br /> <br /> 11) The local Heirarch has just committed Suicide by Banisher. Power vacuum ensues.<br /> <br /> 12) The local Hierarch wants the PCs to figure out what made a hotel room disappear. When the room is observed, it looks at though they're looking out a window--the space that the room should occupy simply doesn't exist.<br /> <br /> 13) A new convergence of ley lines appears over a specific building in the PCs town. Whether these were naturally occurring, but hidden until now, or have been &quot;moved&quot; by another force is unclear... but [i]everyone/i] wants control over them now.<br /> <br /> 14) Last year the consillium was under constant threat from a large cabal of Tremere. After some hefty fighting, the Tremere that weren't killed in battle were publicly tried and executed for their crimes. Now that things are settleing down, Consillium politics resume. But you've been getting short glimpses in public places of executed mages seemingly acting alive and well. For some reason, Councilors and leaders of Order caucuses are ignoring your warnings, or even accusing you of trying to rile up 'troubles'. How do you act?<br /> <br /> 15) After having returned from a trip into the Astral, a Moros PC finds that he is dead. Well, not really, but he has been declared dead by the law. And his relatives and friends are grieving. And there has also been a burial. And there's also a corpse, which appears to be that of the player character, even when looking at it with the most powerful Death Sight spell.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 16) For the last day and a half, no one could order pizza from anywhere in the city, and there is no frozen pizza on the shelves of supermarkets. Any attempts to make pizza seem to go bad--out of ingredients, faulty ovens, and other unintended mishaps. What is it that needs to remove pizza from existence?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 17) One of the Free Companies has wound up in the region overseen by your PC's Consilium. The issue is that the Company seems to be interested in going 'legit', as far as the magical community goes. The cabal has very powerful members, a great deal of occult information and their long-standing mercenary attitude is gaining them allies of convenience. The leader of the Company has even shown interest in taking over a Councilor's seat recently vacated by a retiring mage.<br /> <br /> But can the proponents of amoral warfare be trusted? And why haven't the mainstream Arrow made a move against the noted heretics?<br /> <br /> <br /> 18) It's the Book of the Ladder. One of the most obscure yet important grimoires on the topic of the Supernal and its manifestations. And it's right there on the shelf of a Sleeper bibliophile, who, most certainly, doesn't have the faintest idea of what it's about.<br /> <br /> .. and there's some evidence of Seer magic in and around the house. Something needs to be done.<br /> <br /> 19) Enough is enough. The Guardians of the Veil collectively declare the Free Council in town to be Nefandi and Left-Handed for their refusal to distance themselves from questionable magical practices. The two factions are in a state of open war.<br /> <br /> 20) It's done. The Mysterium has dug up one of the Athaenaea Prima, one of the three lore houses constructed prior to the Fall by fugitives from Atlantis itself; places containing the highest of all mysteries.<br /> <br /> ... and what the Athaenaeum Prima contains are countless books on summoning greater demons, creating gates into the Abyss and religious treatises extolling the virtues of the Abyss.<br /> <br /> This should have been impossible, because at the time when the Athaenaeum Prima was allegedly constructed, the Abyss didn't yet exist.<br /> <br /> .) For the last few weeks, several spirit allies have been bringing warning that a relatively powerful cabal of sorcerers is planning to move into the city. Divinition through fate and time has confirmed this, thought strangely enough, their alliegiances are not revealed. It appears that each of the members of this cabal are protected by occultation and well designed fate spells. When the cabal arrives in town they immediately announce their intent to join the consilium by sending missives through spirit allies and various mundane means.<br /> <br /> When these mages present themselves before the hierarch. They come bringing gifts of tass and even artifacts. It is evident they are wealthy and well connected. Spirits interact with them with respect. Their knowledge of the mysteries is furthermore evident. However, when their auras are put under mage sight, they are off. Vibrant but certainly not mages. The cabal are thaumaturges (from Second Sight) who's belief system is the Atlantian system as taught by the Silver Ladder and Mysterium.<br /> <br /> Who are these sorcerers, and what is the consilium to do with them?<br /> <br /> <br /> 13) You come across a young Awakened child. They are immensely gifted (Gnosis 6+) with an apparently instinctual Mastery of the Prime arcanum but little other knowledge. They have no appreciation for the dangers or limits of magic in the Fallen World. And, of course, the child is pursued. Where did this child come from? Who or what is pursuing them? How do the mages protect this child long-term? And do they want to?<br /> <br /> 14) A psychotic killer escaped custody, the authorities can't explain how - it seems awakened magic was used. Soon there are murders that fit his style. The targets are sleepwalker retainers or lone mages.<br /> <br /> How did he escape and why are his victims sleepwalkers and mages? Had he help from a pylon and used as a distraction? Did he awaken as a banisher or one of the mad?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 21) A Sleeper mystery cult has accidentally stumbled upon Supernal truths resonant with the Supernal Realm of Pandaemonium. It is entirely possible that its key figures will Awaken in the near future.<br /> <br /> Both the Guardians of the Veil and the Silver Ladder have become aware of the mystery cult. The Guardians, having judged the cult unworthy of greater mysteries, intend to infiltrate the cult and prevent Awakenings from taking place, preferably without doing any lasting damage. Agents of the Silver Ladder desire to swell their ranks with new recruits.<br /> <br /> 22) Someone claiming to be the Hieromagus shows up. He's obviously a pretender. Pretty much everyone wants him dead (other than a couple heretics, but then, who asked them?), and the PCs have been selected for the task. They are to infiltrate and destroy the heresy.<br /> <br /> While attempting to do so, the PCs are exposed to evidence that this might really, actually be the messiah of the Guardians of the Veil, come to redeem the order and lead the Awakened into a new age.<br /> <br /> 17) A Free Council cabal of doctors and scientists have been implanting unknowing mortals with a particular form of imbued item in the hopes of creating a new line of Proximi.<br /> <br /> 23) No mage can use Time magic to predict the future further than the 29th of September, 2013. The most powerful Acanthi utterly fail in seeing any future past that date.<br /> <br /> 19) A prison made with normal ( PC usable, non-plot device) magic by a cabal of Masters has been broken. All manner of previously summoned, then captured gulmoth are out in the world wreaking havoc or lying in wait. The cabal that created the prison has disappeared, its members fleeing from vengeful mages and gulmoth (or something else...).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 24) One of the basic cable channels starts broadcasting an infomercial advertising a series of videos which seem to reveal a number of Supernal truths, or at least brush up against them. As if that weren't bad enough, the infomercial features all of the PCs as spokespeople or experts. None of them have any recollection of being involved in this dangerous nonsense, but it may be more than a little difficult to convince the Guardians of the Veil of that....<br /> <br /> 25) A notorious convicted criminal is sentenced to die by electric chair, but his execution is interrupted when he Awakens in the middle of it and uses his new powers to save himself. While the witnesses are unclear on the details (since all of them were Sleepers) the reaction has been sensational--some more excitable types have indicated it's a sign of divine (or Satanic) favor, and even if it weren't, it would be good for weeks of breathless coverage on CNN for being such a strange fluke. Now he's been scheduled to be executed again, and various mages in the community are wondering if he should be rescued rather than left to die. What if he's actually innocent of the charges? And what if he isn't?<br /> <br /> <br /> 20) A local Moros who frequently uses ghosts and has some bound to them (this could even be a PC) has their sanctum attacked by a group of Sin-Eaters who free the ghosts bound to it. The PCs have the job of hunting down this mysterious menace, with the opportunity to perhaps reconsider the standard view of ghosts as a resource.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 21) You find yourself being temporally scried upon from the future... a lot. Your immediate future and destiny are clouded, tangled and otherwise murky. What's about to happen and what can you do about it? And how do you feel about future historians watching your life play out? And is their future history locking down your choices in some fashion?<br /> <br /> 22) An Archmage's Ochema appears in your sanctum and with a smirk says, &quot;Bob fucked up. You get to play.&quot; He tosses you an artifact that positively screams with Supernal resonance. &quot;Try not to get killed too soon, huh?&quot; And without another word, he's gone. Welcome to the Pax Arcanum.<br /> <br /> 22)For years, the city has been celebrating times of prosperity and growth. Awakenings have been steady in rate, new spells and lore have even been discovered and the cabals of the city are at peace. Every mage seems satisfied with the Hierarch's leadership. The one day, all the representatives are gone without a trace. What now?<br /> <br /> <br /> 26) Local spirits start acting more and more unusual. They appear to be hungrier than before.<br /> <br /> If that wasn't enough, they also have formed some sort of truce between their own kind. They have stopped hunting their own kind as food.<br /> <br /> Very soon their hunger will become unbearable.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 27) A migration of deer of no known species and no sense of fear is causing havok through the city, especially given that an influential and powerful mage claims they are of supernal origin and must be protected. Everyone would agree this is incredibly unlikely, except that life spells seem to be causing much less paradox in their vicinity.<br /> <br /> 28) Some recent sleeper drilling work in the central city seems to have unearthed something deep underground, and spines of metal are starting to push up through parks and floors of buildings.<br /> <br /> 29) A previously trusted guardian mage claims he has found a plot within the concilium and that some of it's members are secretly seer aligned, but has broken off all his normal contacts and started recruiting allies in order to fight them, but won't publicly denounce them for some reason. The players are asked to approach him and find out what is going on.<br /> <br /> 30) An artefact has been delivered to the concilium for safe keeping, except that it seems to be attracting large amounts of anger spirits to the area.<br /> <br /> <br /> 25) A reclusive but highly respected apostate who is a master in several of the Arcana arrives at the latest Consilium meeting and announces he will be taking on a single apprentice, To this end he will be observing and testing several prospective candidates over the coming weeks. The Pcs knows this Apostate is vehemently apolitical but he has many enemies in the consilium and becoming his apprentice will likely entail inheriting these enemies of his. Are the rewards worth the risks?<br /> <br /> <br /> 31) The Hierarch's factotum contacts one of the PCs (a low-status Guardian would be best). An Arrow sent on a mission to a disputed nearby metropolis made contact with a Mammon Seer who claims to know the identity of a Panopticon mole in the upper echelons of the Guardian hierarchy. Bring in the Arrow and investigate the story - and if true, identify the mole. If you really want to, you could give the senior Guardians some sort of code name, maybe based on occupation or something.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 26) Several people around the city are kidnapped, held for a few days while being painfully tortured, then released completely unharmed save for their experience. In each case they report that their kidnapper was apologetic and said the experience was necessary to &quot;prepare&quot; them, and they do seem to be more resilient (higher Resolve, Composure and Willpower) for it. Their accounts also make clear that their captor was a mage using a demesne.<br /> <br /> <br /> 32) The local Free Council have elected a proximus as their chairman/representative, the silver ladder (and a few in the mysterium) are up in arms.<br /> <br /> 33) A local cabal has been in dire needs of funds, so they've started cooking meth...<br /> <br /> <br /> 34) The cabal needs to consult a Mysterium mage in the nearest big city, but when they arrive at his sanctum he's missing and nobody has seen him in days. Following the thread of his research they discover a maze of tunnels beneath the city, an entire hidden world that goes deeper and deeper into the earth...<br /> <br /> 35) The cabal gets word that the newly-built high rise skyscraper in town has some connection to the Seers of the Throne and they're tasked to investigate. They were right. It does have a connection. It's a trap. It's an ingenious living prison designed to hold them and recondition them to love the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> 36) The Free Council has been monitoring a local professor who is showing signs of awakening, but now she needs extracting because a dangerous sleeper cult is threatening her. The PCs arrive just in time to save her and she awakens in the middle of the combat...as a banisher.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 37) A Mysterium Egregori has devoted his life to following a certain spirit that radiates peace and light. He tracks down its manifestations in different places, converses with it, records its teachings. The spirit has just manifested on the cabal's turf, and appears to be a force for good...but across town the dead body of another awakened has just been discovered...<br /> <br /> 38) The Guardians of the Veil move to shut down a Free Council UFO cult...but somebody else got there first. All its members appear to be missing. There's video of the leader in front of a crowd of people, disappearing in a flash of light...<br /> <br /> 39) The Consilium library has been burglarized. Some priceless volumes are missing. The cabal tracks the thieves far out into the sticks where a crowd is gathered around an enormous bonfire. They're burning books.<br /> <br /> 40) After the publication of a few highly popular occult novels, a fascination with occultism and mysticism in general has become mainstream. Societies such as the Rosicrucians and the Freemasons are more popular than ever; and Labyrinths, Cryptopoli and Seer cults have received a vast influx of new members. Consequently, the number of Awakenings per year has increased significantly.<br /> <br /> The Silver Ladder sees this as their great opportunity to move to the next step of their plan to break the Lie and defeat the pretender gods. The Seers of the Throne, on the other hand, are frothing with rage, behaving highly irrational and not at all far away from taking drastic action that might endanger all the Awakened.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 41) When a little girl from the mainland goes missing, clues lead the authorities to a tiny island off the coast inhabited by a proximi cult of the Silver Ladder. The proximi swear they know nothing, the police are demanding answers, and both sides are being very uncooperative.<br /> <br /> 28) During a contentious and controversial trial in the Consilium, an ally of the cabal's unleashes a powerful attack spell that injures several mages and gives the accused an opportunity to escape. Your cabal's ally swears that it wasn't his intention, that an outside force triggered one of his prepared spells against his will. He is well-known for carrying such prepared spells and there is some Prime resonance that could support his story but it's not enough to make a convincing case for innocence by itself. He needs your help to prove his innocence while a divided Consilium debates how to respond both to his actions and the fugitive's escape. Obviously, whoever planned this escape will not want the cabal digging into it.<br /> <br /> 29) For three months, a string of increasing, yet mundane annoyances has been plaguing the city's Awakened population. Parking tickets, loss of electricity and phone service, backed up plumbing, the works! And not only are the Pentacle and Seers affected, but several powerful Scelesti entrenched in city government have been hit as well. At first they just killed the repo men come to collect their belongings, but when a week later the same repo men came to visit (with no apparent consequences from or memories of the previous encounter), it was clear that something was seriously wrong.<br /> <br /> 42) The Hegemonic Ministry, in a desperate attempt to reclaim its leadership position of the Seers of the Throne, has begun a vast terraform project in the Astral Realm. Symbols of control and submittance are weaved into every Temenos realm the Hegemons get their hands on. Already, Sleepers in any given location start acting with a little less free will day after day.<br /> <br /> 43)The Seers have, as one, gone insane. They've been attacking one another openly, using hideously conspicuous vulgar magic with wild abandon. They stole the Smithsonian Institute! The whole building! For a day and a half, they went insane.<br /> <br /> Then, at two minutes to midnight Zulu, at points scattered across the globe, there were detonations, ranging from incendiary to nuclear to whatever that was off the coast of Singapore.<br /> <br /> And then it stopped. Then it started getting strange. Junior Seers and bold Pentacle mages searching abandoned strongholds and burned-out palaces find that every senior member of every Ministry and every even vaguely movable asset, along with every member of their inner circles not identified as dead or captured in the intervene fighting, is gone.<br /> <br /> &quot;Iteration fail confirmed. Evacuation of assets by Omega Zeta Three is in effect. Confirm denial of assets before departures. Pickup is at Midnight Zulu. Repeat, Iteration fail confirmed.&quot;<br /> <br /> 45) A respected member of the Consilium has apparently gone insane. He claims he has been contacted by an Angel of fire and eyes, and that he must purge the Consilium. He needs to be stopped.<br /> <br /> 46) The CDC is int own, looking at a recent epidemic that has struck the poorer parts of town. And they've been asking too many questions about Pentacle interests.<br /> <br /> 47) Three persons have now been apparently attacked by a Pteranodon. The last one was actually killed. Authorities want the creature killed, but the Mysterium wants it captured so they can study it.<br /> <br /> 48) A new forest has appeared near the town. It is hungry.<br /> <br /> .) Walk past the alleys of Siem Reap's Night Market. Open your third eye to the Arcanum of crude matter, and perhaps, if the Exarchs permit, you'll find a doorway that isn't there. It might take you to the temple of a true god.<br /> <br /> It is possibly the only temple of the Exarch known as the Chancellor that welcomes all mages, even those of the Pentacle. His High Priest, a Seer of the Throne who calls himself the Merchant, has never been known to refuse Pentacle mages entry.<br /> <br /> Violence is impossible in the Chancellor's temple - it is a place of worship to the Chancellor.<br /> <br /> Pentacle Mages dare enter the Exarch's sanctum because they desire what conventional means cannot provide. Here they find a Merchant willing to fulfill their needs, provided that the price is right.<br /> <br /> Everything is for sale in the Chancellor's temple. Guns, rotes, artifacts, Awakened souls, Sleepers without souls (empty shells, hollowed out) - everything. The price is always more than the Pentacle mages are willing to pay, and it always involves some sort of ritual offering to the Chancellor.<br /> <br /> <br /> 32) Seemingly at random, the consciousness of people around the city are exchanging bodies. Whatever is causing it is not Unravelling and not wearing off. The Consilium and the local Seer pylons have a tacit agreement to suppress awareness of the situation until it can be resolved; this does not always end well for the victims. However, the more people it happens to, the harder it becomes to cover up.<br /> <br /> 33) People around the city begin uncontrollably expressing extremes of emotion: wracking sobs, hysterical laughter, mindless rage, transports of joy and so on. It persists even when they sleep and is utterly debilitating in terms of their ability to lead their lives or even care for themselves. It's also upsetting the balance of the local spirit-realms.<br /> <br /> 50) Over some months of game time, hint at some turf war in the shadows. Free Council statistical analysts have noted that there have been an unlikely number of gas main explosions in the city, that more cars are burning after accidents than is usual outside Hollywood, that there are a surprising number of incidents of spontaneous human combustion in the early morning, that animal attacks are on the rise, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Finally, the PCs' cabal are approached by a vampire and a werewolf - can they provide neutral ground for the Prince and the Alpha to negotiate an end to the war between their two factions?<br /> <br /> On the night in question, of course, someone will have the bright idea of wiping out both high commands when they are outside of their home turf, plus there will be the usual divertissements -<br /> <br /> one aide is possessed by a Seer looking to cause trouble.<br /> there's a Furry-Romeo-and-Undead-Juliet subplot. Help, hinder, or point-and-laugh as you see fit.<br /> someone else is trying to sell out their boss (a lieutenant of one of the leaders) and use the other side to ensure their own promotion by assassination<br /> one of the delegates is someone who has a blood feud with a PC but is protected by the cabal's promise of safe conduct<br /> another cabal wants to harm a leader and thereby cause the PCs to lose face,<br /> the PCs inadvertently pick a location for the talks that has a previously-unnoticed Thing In The Cellar<br /> one leader cannot just stop the fighting - s/he is under pressure from a faction of their own splat to ensure that there is not peace in our time, and needs the PCs help to get away with an armistice.<br /> the local Athenaum has a really cool ritual that just needs 20cc of vampire blood to run - could a PC get some?<br /> a senior Arrow is an enthusiastic hunter and would really like to put a nice wolf pelt in the trophy room. Can the PCs arrange for a suitable victim to be available for pursuit?<br /> a senior officer in the Consilium (and/or a PCs mentor) has a fetish for being bitten. Maybe the PCs could ensure things don't get out of hand while they scratch that particular itch<br /> one werewolf has taken rather a lot of initiative and opened talks with an out-of-town bunch of rogue Awakened terrorists who have developed a biological weapon that affects vampires, and hopes to acquire and deploy it at the talks. Who knows what effects it really has, both on the intended targets, and on anyone else who comes into contact with the Infected.<br /> <br /> Go wild, really.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 51) A reality TV contestent seems to be on the verge of awakening, he's been talking about how the world they're in seems so unreal, using supernal symbolism to describe &quot;the audience&quot;, and experienced cultors think he's close. Your guardian PC is asked to get him out of there subtly before he causes some vulgar magic on live TV.<br /> <br /> 52. The cabal discovers a small town where every single citizen is a puppet of one very powerful Seer. He can take control of any of them at any time, and he can exert less-fine control over entire mobs of them. The solution is simple: take out the Seer. But there are hundreds of townsfolk between the Seer and the cabal. And what is this town protecting or hiding?<br /> <br /> 51. A chunk of the Supernal realm of Stygia fell (slid? warped?) to earth outside Toledo, Ohio yesterday. The mountains are moving. The dead are walking. And the manifestation is sucking the mana dry from every hallow in a 50 mile radius.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Your boss is being an asshole. There are a million ways to making him suffer a little using magic.<br /> <br /> You need money. Lots of it, and now. In the absence of a job - you lost your old job while Awakening - the only thing to do is to steal it.<br /> <br /> You begin to suspect that your girlfriend is cheating on you. Will you be using magic to spy on her? Will you tamper with her mind to make sure she still loves you?<br /> <br /> Your brother has somehow pissed off a bunch of very scary people - the kind that carries automatic weapons. He needs help, now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 54) The village of Cootseby in Cambridgeshire is at first glance the perfect English village. A genial retired major organizes games of cricket on the green. The wife of the local vicar runs a painfully earnest Metaphysical Society for discussions of Swedenborg and Madame Blavatsky, and the church hall hosts fetes and amateur theatricals and musical variety evenings (\u201cOur next guest, the very talented Mr. Tobias Simes, will perform a medley drawn from the oeuvre of Messrs Gilbert &amp; Sullivan\u2026\u201d). Everything is pleasant, normal and picturesque.<br /> <br /> But any visitor who ventures out at night discovers a very different Cootesby \u2013a dark, horrifying place haunted by sinister, masked figures, a Satanic, bestial orgy of lust, intrigue, witchcraft and violence. The village is filled with whispered secrets, rumours of potential escape and awful mysteries -investigation of any of them will drag the mage through the village' heaving, dark underbelly, filled with repulsive, psychotic characters; twisted versions of the village's daytime inhabitants, and dark, incomprehensible schemes. And in the morning, all is back to prim, wholesome reality.<br /> <br /> Cootesby is the creation of the Banisher known as Caligari. He drugs and kidnaps mages and transports them here. The village is a prison camp intended to condition the mages brought there by causing them to associate dreams, magic, curiosity and fantasies with nightmarish suffering and revulsion and to force them to embrace the dull, prosaic safety represented by the daytime Cootesby. Once a mage has given into Cootesby, participates fully in the \u2018life of the village\u2019 and has stopped wandering around at night and trying to investigate any of its mysteries, they are whisked back to their previous life, stripped all of their passion, their pride and their power.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 55) There isn't, nor has there ever been, a Sixth order of the Pentacle. Anyone claiming otherwise is clearly an abyssal mage trying to tear us apart, and must be dealt with immediately.<br /> <br /> 56) There isn't an evil you in an alternate reality similar to our own. There's 4 different yous, one for each tower, the realities intertwined like a pentacle. And one of them just fell into our reality after a paradox backlash.<br /> <br /> 57) An old Moros has recently died, and has left his personal library to any kingdom who can survive a week in his old creepy mansion up the hill.<br /> <br /> 58) A strange man has appeared in the local poor neighborhood, apparently selling magical powers to anyone who meets his prize. And it seems like it really works. He must be stopped.<br /> <br /> 59) A renowned sleeper archaeologist currently staying at a local university has apparently discovered ancient artifacts from Atlantis. And is about to make his findings public.<br /> <br /> 60) A very potent celestial alignment si supposed to occur soon that will cause the city's ley lines to become charged with supernal power. And everyone's trying to get ready for it.<br /> <br /> 36) There's a new superhero in town! Vague reports keep coming in and videos showing up on the Internet of a costumed vigilante apparently using superpowers to fight locathe city have twisted into a knot and the energy is going somewhere. Resonance near the knot is extremely volatile and changes all the time. If the mages figure out a way to trace where the energy is going it turns out to be under the ice in Antarctica.<br /> <br /> 64. Mages throughout the city have had experiences seeing an entity in their mirrors that stare them in the eyes and psychically project a demand to know if they are [insert name of NPC here]. Recollections by the victims are hazy. The longer this goes on the more intrusive the questioning becomes, and the victims start to get headaches and bleed from the nostrils. No spirit magic can detect a trace of anything actually being there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 65) A local factory sacks all their workers but keeps going on as if nothing has happened. No one from the old factory is brave enough to contest it for some reason.<br /> (I particularly imagine this as an abyssal manifestation)<br /> <br /> 66) A mage from the concilium is fading out of people's memories, starting most quickly with those that have known him longest, he asks for your assistance in working out the origin of the effect, and acting as his intermediaries in the meantime.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 67) Everything is fine and nothing is going wrong. At all.<br /> 68) You have received a letter from the IRS informing you that you are a few years behind on your magic taxes.<br /> 69) A ancient grimoire has found itself in the hands of a not particularly bright street gang. And somehow they're using it to cast spells to strengthen their turf.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 70) Somewhere in southern Thailand, Sleepers have dug up dinosaur bones that look unlike all others. Except that there are a couple things that are really different from &quot;ordinary&quot; dinosaur bones. For one, they're much older.<br /> <br /> Very soon, people start dying near the bones, their bodies displaying gigantic claw marks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 71) A long time ago, in a reality far, far far away, it was a time of civil war.<br /> Free Council mages, striking from a hidden base, have won their first victory against the SEERS OF THE THRONE. During the battle, Council spies managed to steal the plans to the Exarchs' ultimate weapon, the ManaStar, an armored battle station with enough firepower to destroy an entire city. Pursued by the Seers' sinister agents, Maga Leia races home aboard her airship, custodian of the stolen plans that can save her people and restore freedom to the Fallen World.<br /> <br /> The PCs get hints of an Atlantean object that was used in the Nameless War. Additional research liberates a mage's skull found with glyphs that imply &quot;MacGuffin here&quot; and cleverly determine that a really good way to find it would be to use the crystal skull as a link to the mage's oneiros... where they find themselves in a 1930s pulp all-action spectacular. You might as well just run A New Hope straight but shorn of its science-fantasy/space opera stylings, with a giant double-enveloped airship that mounts a directed-mana weapon that is more Independence Day than Doc Savage.<br /> <br /> The catch is, of course, that the ManaStar directed-mana weapon plans will actually work if built in the real world, and are for an artifact that can actually level a city if deployed appropriately (like, from an aircraft some miles away).<br /> <br /> Are there morality consequences for jacking out as soon as you have the plans, knowing that the Hierarch will destroy the Nameless Base on the outskirts of Yavinton?<br /> <br /> 72) Earthdawn<br /> An Atlantean mage family could see the writing on the wall, and built for their children/apprentices a doomsday bunker to survive the Fall. Unfortunately the Fall seems to have had an effect on the bunker's enchantments, because when the PCs find it (more by accident than by design, unless they retrieve other Atlantean records from the adults that identify how to find it), it is still in time suspension. So it's a treasure trove of Atlantean goodies, but probably quite prosaic ones, because it is as much a nursery as it is a caern. Do the PCs want to wake the children out of time and see what secrets they may know? Is it worth the risk? Were the builders pro- or anti-Exarch?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 73). A Day Of Wonder<br /> The Oracles (or somebody) has managed to achieve a minor cosmological victory in the Ascension War, banishing the influence of the Abyss on the Phenomenal World for a whole day. During that day there will be no paradox, all abyssal entities become dormant and powers derived from the Abyss won't function, and everyone would basically be a Sleepwalker for that day, able to remember magic they witness clearly.<br /> How do different mage factions take advantage of this metaphysical circumstance? What sort of tactics do the Seers use to counter Pentacle operations to take advantage of the day? What sort of troubles ensue in the world?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 74) A small child seems to be having the obsessive assistance of a mage, with significant evidence of mind magic on all their surrounding acquaintances to remove anything that might threaten them. The resonance doesn't match any mage known to the concilium, and there is something very odd about it. The cabal is charged with identifying this mage and bringing them into the open, so as to identify if they form some kind of threat.<br /> <br /> 75) A free council mage has been working on an advanced technomagic ritual for a few months, and has been trying to use computers to automate sections of it. Unfortunately, one of the computers he was on has been hacked, throwing something off, and he now doesn't have a clue what it's actually doing. He brings you in for a second opinion. His theories of magic seem to be pushing the edge of atlantian metaphysics and not really make much sense, but he's obviously managed to get the computers doing something.<br /> <br /> 76) There are signs of a reaper attack in the local area, and during the investigation your are approached by a young mage, he says that the evidence will point to him, but he is being framed by his master, who he will lead you to.<br /> <br /> 77) A series of mundane coincidences are hampering organisation in the concilium, and they start to become ridiculous. Some blame the exarchs, other archmaster fate magic, but what could be happening that they'd put in this much effort?<br /> <br /> 78) Your future self is constantly going back in time, trying to manipulate you, get you to do certain things. Its actions are getting more and more desperate, and it simply refuses to explain them.<br /> <br /> 79) A spirits start following you around. It appears to be friendly - it's obvious that it wants you to take it as a familiar. What are its motives?<br /> <br /> 80) An educational foundation has come to the concilium's attention, because of the extreme spooky uniformity of the people involved. As far as can be told the seers are not involved, and given how interested they'd be, it cannot be around for them to find.<br /> <br /> 81) An arrow mage has been fomenting rivalry between two local football teams, in the hope that the competition will lead to awakenings. It's getting a little of out hand, but he's said he'll do it until someone awakens.<br /> <br /> 82) Someone has been stealing from the Athenaeum, and your cabal have been tasked with forming an extra line of defence while higher status others try to get their stuff back. (Yes, guard duty isn't a great hook, but good for building a sense of place you can use in the future)<br /> <br /> 83) An old city alderman has been recently recognised as a powerful independent mage from before the formation of the free council, and people are going back through old history in order to work out what he left behind.<br /> <br /> 84) A powerful mage contacts you for information about your mentor, although rather than manoeuvring, they actually seem to be in love with them and asking for advice, they're very incompatible however, and this could easily result in a feud.<br /> <br /> 85) A plane has just landed at the airport without any of it's passengers or flight attendants, the pilots seem completely unaware that anything had happened.<br /> <br /> .) The local river spirit demands yearly sacrifices - in human bodies, obviously. It is way too powerful to be strongarmed into ceasing to demand its sacrifices.<br /> <br /> It's that time of the year again and the orders need its sacrifices, or else the river might express its anger by causing some catastrophe. Someone needs to do something.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 42) In the University of Pennsylvania's Museum of Archeology &amp; Anthropology, in the Chinese exhibit area, stand two stone Qilin (lion-dragons) facing the center of the room, appearing to recoil in horror from what stands there. In the center of the room in a glass case, atop a silver wave, is a flawless crystal ball. What images does its surface show, and is it a coincidence that the two qilin, statues who in the past would guard from spirits, seem to be rearing back from it?<br /> <br /> (Actually how it is at that museum, was there for the first time in around a decade, wonderful place, so many WoD plots can be made from it. This one alone can go well in any venue)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 87) You wake up to find that you have lost your link to the Watchtower and reverted to being a Sleeper. The same has happened to every single member of your cabal. The entire Consilium of the city seems to have disappeared and no one even remembers you being anything more than you are. But your enemies remain and they want to use this opportunity to finally get rid of you. What is going on? How can you reAwaken? Is is even possible? What happened to rest of the Orders? You have to figure out what to do while trying not be killed by gods.<br /> <br /> 88) An ally of the cabal suddenly gains power in leaps and bounds until he ascends to the Supernal World as an Archmaster. Ever since then, you have been having strange dreams and seeing omens everywhere. Is he trying to tell you something? How did he Ascend so quickly anyhow?<br /> <br /> 89) Your cabal is approached by a man claiming to be immortal, having been alive for millenia. He wishes to die. Death or Life Arcana magic reveals nothing special about him, but when he blows his brains out with a gun in front of you and then wakes again moments later, you are forced to believe him. How is this possible? Do you even want to help him, given the treasure trove of knowledge that must be his head? And what is he so frightened of, given he can't die?<br /> <br /> 90) There is a new fast food chain in town. It appeared out of nowhere and within weeks won over hundreds of customers with its catchy jingles, colourful mascots and tasty food. Then a mage you all know dies and investigation reveals that the last place he visited was one of the fast food outlets. The food in his stomach has curdled into foul-smelling black ash. What is going on here?<br /> <br /> .) The PCs are struggling with a Hierarch and a Consilium of a particularly reactionary orientation. The Hierarch is a tyrant; things that the PCs have on their todo-list have been outlawed by the Consilium.<br /> <br /> This is when the PCs are contacted by members of a Nameless order with an invitation to participate in a conspiracy to overthrow the Pentacle orders in town.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 92) Someone was publically assasinated with a mind effect spell, the mage who's resonance applies to it is dead, and besides that, there's now an investigation that needs redirecting (I'm thinking imbued item weapon used by sleepers)<br /> <br /> 93) People in the local area are dreaming that all the trees and lamposts outside their houses are strung with televisions, blasting static. They can't sleep.<br /> <br /> 94) A member of one of the PCs' family seems to be on the road to awakening, but keeping shadow identities seperate is particularly important in this city.<br /> <br /> 44) The mutilated corpse of a well known Sleepwalker retainer of a counciler is found in the characters Sanctum. The wounds suggest the retainer was ritually sacrificed to reap mana. The characters have bearly time to notice the body, when the Sentinels, tasked from the counciler with finding the retainer, arrive.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 95) After a random act of kindness done by a PC, the recipient turns out to be an archmaster in disguise. He intends to reward the PC - he'll Awaken any one Sleeper of the PC's choosing.<br /> <br /> The PC is to decide within 24 hours.<br /> <br /> It's all, ultimately, a test of the PC's wisdom. Sleepers who aren't ready to Awaken naturally do so as Banishers. The PC wins by refusing to select a Sleeper.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 96) A young woman recently Awoke - and pretty much all Acanthi in the city felt it. It doesn't take much training in the Fate Arcanum to perceive the incredibly strong strands of destiny suffusing her pattern. The auguries are clear - she will be very beneficial to the goals of her order.<br /> <br /> Except that she hasn't yet joined any of the orders. And the auguries kinda don't say which order she'll end up in.<br /> <br /> They all want her. Even the Seers of the Throne. The PCs have been selected to make the sales pitch for their respective orders.<br /> <br /> <br /> 97) A crime spree affects the PCs' cabal. Their locale is seeing a rise in burglary and armed robbery rates - they or their Sleeper associates are affected. Have a slow buildup here mostly as asides in other storylines' sessions.<br /> <br /> They need gas but the gas station nearby is closed as the cops are investigating a holdup and shooting.<br /> They can't get served because the store or restaurant is understaffed because some of them have been arrested for stealing from the cash register.<br /> A PC's apartment is ransacked - anything magical is ignored, but the TV, stereo, jewelry, cash, computers, and DVDs or music are taken - as may be other Sleeper associates if they have mundane day jobs. This may cause complications if the hard drives or USB memory sticks also have something magical on them.<br /> The girl bagging their groceries has a black eye - a colleague passing by asks what happened and she tells of a home invasion by armed robbers.<br /> They are stopped at traffic lights and witness a carjacking of the vehicle in front of them.<br /> A night-time meeting at a club finishes without incident, but as they are driving away, a van passes them to do a drive-by on the line of waiting clubgoers (which accidentally wings one of the people they were meeting with), as another gang wants to take over the distribution business.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Further investigation reveals that this appears to be a mundane and random issue - the offenders were solely motivated by a desire for money, as they have serious narcotics addiction problems (this may be street dealers selling to the underclass; if a nice group of doctors prescribing under-the-counter Vicodin or Percoset, then the crime is more likely something white-collar and stupid, like someone slamming on the brakes to make a whiplash and inflated bodywork damage claim.)<br /> <br /> Even further investigation reveals that the dealers of the narcotics in question are part of the revenue stream of a Pentacle mage or cabal - one in good standing in the Consilium, who have determined that this is an acceptable revenue stream under the leges magicarum that apply locally (it is not the dealer cabal, nor their direct agents, who are harming the PCs' area - it is their agents' customers, and there is a precedent in a previous Consilium ruling that this is a great enough degree of separation for responsibility to not fall upon the dealer mages), and are not inclined to cease operations. The dealers' may be using Matter or Forces to create their product - they are not, however, using Mind or Fate to increase its addiction.<br /> <br /> How do the PCs respond?<br /> <br /> 98) An apprentice of the PC's mentor has gone Left-Handed. The PC must now contend with a mage whose abilities, strategies and way of thinking are functionally very similar to his own.<br /> <br /> <br /> 99) The Malamauda are a New Guinean people who have had next to no contact with modern civilization. They are also entirely unaffected by the Sleeping Curse. More than a third of the (less than 1000) Malamauda are Proximi; all of them are Sleepwalkers. There is something in their ancestry that keeps away the Quiescence.<br /> <br /> 100. Everyone in the Guardians of the Veils Labyrinth in the cabals city suddenly Awakens and most of the Guardians vanish. A few of the Guardians are found dead later.<br /> <br /> 101) Seer activity has skyrocketed in the last couple days. Captured Seers admit, under torture, that they entire order is collectively looking for something called a &quot;Key&quot;, as per the orders of the Exarch known as the Father. Noone really knows what a &quot;Key&quot; is, including the Seers.<br /> <br /> Twist: it's one of the PCs.<br /> <br /> <br /> 50) Something odd is going on. All Sleepwalkers in the city get sick and from this moment on, everyone who would awaken dies in the process through various causes (an awakening man might step into traffic during a mystery play, a woman goes into visions as she awakens but simply doesn't wake up any more).<br /> Is this permanent? Is it caused by the Exarchs and their pawns or is it the Abyss creeping in? Is the characters city the only one or are there other instances?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-01-2020, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T07:13:20-08:00","id":19158,"title":"","content":"102) The pope is about to issue a new bill. Individual mage factions, among them the Silver Ladder and the Paternoster, do what they can to use their influence in the Holy See. The Paternoster want an internally divided church that, at the same time, keeps Sleepers complacent and busy with worshipping lies. The Silver Ladder does what it can to counter the Paternoster's influence.<br /> There is a secret war going on between various mage factions, and the PCs are right in the midst of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T12:27:32-08:00","id":62370,"title":"","content":"103) Whenever an Apprentice Acanthus casts a Fate spell, the result is achieved as a result of someone's death. She finds someone to talk to because they came here to mourn the death of a loved one. She gets to work on time because the street lights malfunction, letting her get through on a green light, but leaving fatal traffic accidents in her wake. She curses an annoying person to leave her alone, and he winds up in the obituary the next day.<br /> <br /> She's extremely worried and is afraid to use her magic. Is this &quot;coincidence&quot;? A curse? Is someone intentionally orchestrating these events? Has Fate been lazy on karmic destiny, using her magic as an opportunity to catch up and balance its books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 01-31-2014, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T09:45:01-07:00","id":140637,"title":"","content":"104) Someone's killing people. Not just any people - bad people. The worst of all criminals; sex offenders, pedophiles, that sort of thing. In gruesome ways.<br /> <br /> At the same time, your dreams tell you that the Knife Man is drawing closer to the Phenomenal World, with every sacrifice in his name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T19:41:41-07:00","id":154465,"title":"","content":"105) Something has the PC's on edge. They've been hearing about a string of attacks on neighboring cities that target entire cabals of Mages. The movements of the attacks seem to be forming some kind of pattern on the map, as if preparing for a ritual of tremendous scale. When the attacks begin in the PC's city, they discover two things. First, the attacks are the work of a Lich. Second, the Lich brought friends! Not only must the PC's struggle to put down an enemy cabal, but they also have the figure out what kind of ritual they are trying to perform, and hopefully stop it before it's completion. Their city is the last visit needed to complete the pattern and unleash their dark plan upon the country.<br /> <br /> <br /> (Full Metal Alchemist inspired. :P )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T18:35:27-07:00","id":155348,"title":"","content":"106) While depositing an item in the Atheneum (sp?) after a day of study, an Acanthus Mystagogue notices a faint *ping* at the barest edge of his senses. Following the sensation leads him into the more secured section. Investigating further brings him to a mechanical device stored in a block of frozen Time. It seems to have adapted to its confinement, <i>and </i><i>is calling for help.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":1642,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","user":"Paddon","date":". 06-01-2014, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T08:40:08-07:00","id":155662,"title":"","content":"107.) The barista at the local cafe has been having problems containing her anger lately. She's not normally this angry--her history indicates no sign of abuse or other causes for repressed rage (though she is noted to have been adopted). A Thyrsus might note her pattern fluctuating as the month progresses, or nuisance spirits surrounding her. Everything comes to a head when, during a chance encounter with the PCs, she First Changes. Whoops!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T20:44:36-07:00","id":158629,"title":"","content":"108) Last night, something happened to the mages of the city. Their mana was jacked up so high, their wealth of magic appears to be limitless. Most people don't understand the reason behind it, but for those with the power to see the unseen, the reason becomes clear. Every inch of the city is flooded in magical energy that grants all mages within it a nearly limitless supply of mana. Casting a spell requires little more effort than merely scooping a handful of the energy surrounding them like it was a bubble bath!. The source of all this magic is up in the sky, a gigantic portal covering the city. The mana is cascading over the city like a waterfall. On the other side of the portal is an enormous tower, but none of the 5 Mages recognizes it's design from their previous Awakenings. Rumors explode that this portal shows the Unknown Tower, and that the portal leads to the supernal realms!<br /> <br /> But now those who can see it notice that the portal is shrinking a little more everyday. It's closing, and when it does the infinite Mana supply will dry up. So the question is: Do the PC's attempt to find a way to cross through the portal to a realm of limitless power, or will try to speed up the process for fear of the power falling into the wrong hands?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T09:36:17-07:00","id":159140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/11947-1001-mage-story-hooks?p=158629#post158629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But now those who can see it notice that the portal is shrinking a little more everyday. It's closing, and when it does the infinite Mana supply will dry up. So the question is: Do the PC's attempt to find a way to cross through the portal to a realm of limitless power, or will try to speed up the process for fear of the power falling into the wrong hands?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or will they try to make a grab for power while the infinite mana is available?<br /> <br /> <br /> And since I posted:<br /> <br /> 109) [MAGE/DEMON] One of the players' mortal friends/Retainers whom they've helped protect in the past has suddenly had a change of personality. They've become emotionally flat, secretive, and paranoid. They've started poking their nose into the Mages' other friends, their business fronts, and their connections. What's happened is their friend/Retainer once made a Soul Pact with one of the Unchained for security and powerful friends, and the Demon tied them to the players. How do the PCs react to their friend suddenly and irrevocably being obliterated from existence? How do they react when they realize they were unwittingly the playthings in the machinations of another Supernatural? Do they recruit their newfound ally, do they take vengence, do they get involved in the intrigue?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T02:43:54-07:00","id":161515,"title":"","content":"110) The Exarchs are bastards, yes? They're icons of human evil, the epitome of selfishness and hubris.<br /> <br /> It is speculated by some mystagogues that not all of the mages who would eventually become Exarchs feel the same way about humanity. There could, conceivably, be an Exarch who doesn't feel the same desire to control the world of men that his peers experience.<br /> <br /> If such an Exarch were to exist, he'd probably hide his (its?) personal beliefs very well - other Exarchs would consider them to be heresy. He would probably operate with at least as much caution as the Gate - subtly influencing the Seers, pushing them towards a more human approach in their methods, using the tools of control for the greater benefit of the human race.<br /> <br /> The mystagogues feel the need to point out that this is all idle speculation - it is widely known that the Exarchs and their servants cannot be trusted. It is far too likely that a Seer of the Throne who claims to have goals similar to the Pentacle is a liar.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T03:58:43-07:00","id":161556,"title":"","content":"111) Strange people in dark grey nondescript suits have been spotted around town, claiming to be from the Department of Undisclosed Sciences. They're not making any real trouble,t heir credentials flag responses from the right databases and they don't seem supernatural, but they're taking strange 'readings' from parts of town, and always stare at any mage who walks by...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T13:21:08-07:00","id":202336,"title":"","content":"112) Last night, for approximately 3 minutes, every normal human in the city became Awakened, before returning to Sleepers and forgetting the incident. The humans may not realize what happened, but the resident Mages are demanding answers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T14:04:42-07:00","id":203240,"title":"","content":"113) There's a new hallucinogen on the streets. That's no surprise, you're city's been the place for drug runners for decades. What is surprising is that long time abusers of this drug have a tendency to Awaken while on their drug trips! Is this a completely accidental side effect, or is somebody intentionally trying to create more Mages. If it's the former, then fine, just get rid of the drug before things get too out of hand. If it's the later, then who is behind it... and why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T02:15:14-07:00","id":203648,"title":"","content":"114) A sanctum of a famous 19th century alchemist has recently been discovered. Within were stored various rare grimoires, some enchanted items and a true gem - The Philosophers Stone. Yep. It apparently allows for Paradox free Matter transmutation ! The &quot;potion of immortality&quot; bit hasn't yet been tested yet but lost of people want it. Some want to study it, some want to use it, some think about replicating it. But is it really paradox-free ? And if so why did it's creator ,after discovering such a wondrous thing, keep it hidden instead of showing his briliance to the world ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T09:19:17-07:00","id":203897,"title":"","content":"(Hee, that's simple: The Alchemist used his profound understanding of internal alchemy to Ascend, and the stone is part of his Sarira...)<br /> <br /> 115) Reports of fiery rain and rivers of flame abounded in the distant past, a local Mysterium archivist claims. Apparently, these strange events followed tales of hollow people, easily controlled, and some with missing souls, entirely. The archivist brought this to light because the hollow people have begun to crop up again, and some have claimed to have encountered a few soulless. The Scelestii culprits from before were <i>thought </i>to be completely eradicated, and their tomes destroyed or censored.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T09:45:23-07:00","id":203924,"title":"","content":"I'm not familiar with IM so i have no idea what you're talking about :P<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T15:17:24-07:00","id":205394,"title":"","content":"116)There's a bunch of weirdos in plague doctor uniforms prancing through the streets at all hours of the night. They vanish without a trace during sunrise, but your patience for these yahoos has finally worn out. It's time to figure out what the hell they're doing in the city!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 117) Somebody forgot the magic words before picking up a certain grimoire, because the local Moros have flipped their shit and sealed all entrances and exits to the city's graveyard. They're asking for help, preferably somebody who doesn't mind getting covered in rotting viscera!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T15:55:50-07:00","id":205417,"title":"","content":"118) A Free Council cabal has just opened up a next generation VR lounge. They're not doing a lot of publicity stunts, but the people who have gone rave about just how -real- it all seems. What's actually going on is that the cabal is sponsoring trips into the Astral, paying the mana entrance costs for others and doing some finely tuned mental manipulations to make the transition easier. They have at least one Dreamspeaker who helps to monitor things, and one of the Mages is apparently creating a brand new legacy to further aid in their endeavors. They hope that introducing Sleepers to the Astral will help enlighten and encourage them to explore new possibilities. Something inevitably goes horribly wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T20:50:17-07:00","id":205611,"title":"","content":"(@Menace: I hate to explain jokes, but... when a person ascends, their body goes with them. They often leave behind a sort of mystically significant and magical echo of their body called a Sarira. The parts tend to be magical crystals and such things and have powerful magical effects like artifacts. The joke was crude, albeit in a circuitous way.)<br /> <br /> 119) A Guardian returned from a mission to an Atlantean site oddly quiet. His demeanor prompted Mysterium investigation, but they barely manage to rescue one or two artifacts before the Guardians destroy the site. The site depicted an Ascended King, who ruled in benevolence and wisdom, but also held the body of a traitorous former Mysterium mage who joined the Seers. They wish to understand why the site was so important to obliterate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T09:58:39-07:00","id":951173,"title":"","content":"[Casts Time and/or Death spell on thread]<br /> <br /> 120) The Cabal encounters a decent sized city that seems to have lost connection with the larger Awakened community. When Death Mage Sight is used, they learn that Ghosts are formed <i>far</i> more often than normal. But the city isn't unduly overrun with the spectral dead. Further Investigations yields that the leylines have been modified - any ghost that enters/passes one is drawn along it to the nearest node, which also happens to be a Hallow. Once there, the Ghost's Essence is leeched from them into the Hallow (where it becomes Mana), then they seem to disappear as an Avernian Gate forms. The few ghosts who remain are often far more powerful than normal, though, and use Sleeper proxies to wage a quiet war against their peers in other &quot;territories&quot;. Who modified the leylines this way and why?<br /> <br /> 121) The Cabal gets a lead on an odd lingering mystery from their Order. Upon investigating a small city they make an astonishing discovery - everyone in it has Awakened, at least partially. While there are normal Awakened and Proximi, everyone else has some command over one of the Arcana (treat as Arcana 1, Gnosis 1). However, the Lie seems distorted and strengthened as well - anyone, or indeed, any<i>thing</i> (including information) that leaves the city is subject to alterations of memory and content as per Dissonance, regarding this phenomena in the city. Even the Awakened. Messages sent to Order superiors are altered into revealing nothing about this mass Awakening, local news reports have mundane explanations for magical incidents edited in for viewers outside the city, and even commuters forget their powers upon leaving the city bounds, only remembering them when they re-enter.<br /> <br /> 122) A powerful pulse of Mana pings the Mage Sight of everyone in the Consilium/Assembly in what Mages later call The Imbued Phenomenon. Random people in the area gain &quot;super powers&quot; (A Spell, as if they were an Imbued Item). While these powers seem to provoke the memory altering effects of Quiescence as normal for Supernal Magic, they don't harm Sleepers' souls (no Breaking Point), nor risk Paradox due to witnesses. These Imbued also seem to behave as if they are still Sleepers, being still subject to the Lie to any non-Imbued Supernal magic.<br /> [An excuse to have &quot;superheroes&quot;, with the Cabal cleaning up after their messes.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-16-2016, 09:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T16:18:33-07:00","id":970968,"title":"","content":"<b>123)</b> There's a new Awakened in the city that has everybody (who's in the know) biting their nails in anxiety. Apparently the forces that be went to great lengths to ensure that this mage was kept as docile and ignorant as possible. Projecting subconscious interference that causes them to lose focus of their surroundings, suffer memory lapses, clinical depression, self loathing, doubt, and a bunch of other stuff that might generally hinder somebody's ability to function in society. So when they finally did awaken by accident, all that repressed energy was released like a bomb throughout the city district. Every supernaturally attuned creature instantly felt the power radiating off this guy before it settled down again. Most of the time, he seems calm and collected, but when he feels threatened or provoked, his power erupts into violent outbursts that he has only minor control over.<br /> <br /> You decide to figure out just who this mage is, as well as the source behind his astounding font of power. And if in the process you can figure out a way to tap it for your own, all the better. You'd better hurry, though. Somebody did not want this guy to become a mage, and they most likely aren't going to sit around and let his powers develop any further than they already have!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-16-2016, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T08:23:09-07:00","id":973866,"title":"","content":"<b>124)</b> An incident of mass soul-distortion has the Consilium/Assembly on edge for Reapers. It seems like a staggering number of people had their souls tampered with almost overnight. Some fear an undetected infiltration of Reapers on an unprecedented scale. It doesn't help when investigators detect the Nimbi of a number of new Mages upon the Sleepers affected. The neophyte Mages claim they were investigating as well, and just fouled up and contaminated the Mystery in their own attempts at Revelation.<br /> <br /> [The Idea I had behind this (which you can take or leave, in whole or in part) was: A Mad One lurks in the sewers of the city, having enchanted the pipes to preserve all biological material that enters them until it passes into their care. Using the material, they've forged a staggering network of sympathetic links to everyone who has ever used a toilet in that section of the sewer system. But pursuing their Obsession led them to where they needed the help of an Echo Walker. They bartered for what they needed by allowing the Echo Walker the use of their network, which is what triggered the incident.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-21-2016, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T13:15:56-07:00","id":1084660,"title":"","content":"<b>125)</b> The place the Cabal has traveled to is home to a great - if frustrating - Mystery. Every day, with the tolling of the town clock tower, a powerful wave of magic surges over the area, dispelling most active spells (treat it as a high, though not unbeatable, dispel/Clash of Wills). Only a few, precious, coveted Hallows are unaffected by the wave. Local mages have reconciled themselves to dealing with short term spells, and many have exploited the &quot;free cleanup&quot; by unsafely Relinquishing spells with little care. But what is the source of this recurring dispel? An Artifact? The workings of an Archmaster? Something stranger? And what would happen if it suddenly stopped?<br /> <br /> <b>126)</b> An old, powerful Master recently died. As quickly becomes evident, they were quietly keeping a number of monsters and dangerous phenomena contained. Thankfully, not all of their spells are undone - they cultivated a large group of Sleepwalkers to carry many of the spells responsible. Except someone is tracking <i>them</i> down and murdering them, one by one. As each falls, more and more binding spells become undone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-27-2017, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T13:55:50-07:00","id":1084680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/11947-1001-mage-story-hooks?p=1084660#post1084660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thankfully, not all of their spells are undone - they cultivated a large group of Sleepwalkers to carry many of the spells responsible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given how banner-bearing works is not unlike the extra space a Sanctum provides (plus the necessity of a sympathetic connection to a mage who now no longer exists), I don't think Sleepwalkers can stably sustain an unrelinquished spell beyond its caster's death. The bigger problem is going to be whatever spells they sustained that were affecting <i>them</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>127)</b> Something's drawing some of the spirits of the city to an abandoned warehouse used as a meeting space by a local cult. Once more than one spirit is within the building's walls, none of them can leave \u2014 whether physically or by discorporation \u2014 until one of them has consumed all of the others. It's not clear what attracts a spirit to the warehouse to begin with, as the cult seems as Shadow-blind as the average Sleeper and the building itself is spiritually barren, but spirits related to the cult's members and the &quot;winners&quot; of previous bouts seem to be the most common victims of the process. Stranger still, the latest victor \u2014 a greater Jaggling of unpalatable resonance \u2014 has neither left the warehouse nor been engaged by subsequent challengers; the Shadow of the building is piled high with the unmoving Corpus of starving spirits. What's at work here? Has the champion disrupted the Mystery, or has a new phase of the process been set into motion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T07:19:49-07:00","id":1085012,"title":"","content":"128) While tracking a Sleeper they think is close to Awakening the Cabal is drawn into his Mystery Play as actors. Its a Mastigos Awakening and Hell is whispering in the PCs ears, telling each one of a step on the road he has to take to succeed. The Acanthus has to get him angry enough to murder someone, then present him with the opportunity to do it and get away with it. The Mastigos has to make him fall head over heels in love with him, only to utterly dash his hopes and tear up his illusions. The Moros comes last, he has to to remind him of his greatest fear, then give him the choice of mastering it or dying. If all three succeed, he awakens, if one fails he doesnt make it and settles as a Sleepwalker forever. The players could use magic to assist, but know that throwing spells directly at his pattern in his current state will screw everything up. They have 12 hours to make this happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T12:32:21-07:00","id":1085099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/11947-1001-mage-story-hooks?p=1085012#post1085012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">128) While tracking a Sleeper they think is close to Awakening the Cabal is drawn into his Mystery Play as actors. Its a Mastigos Awakening and Hell is whispering in the PCs ears, telling each one of a step on the road he has to take to succeed. The Acanthus has to get him angry enough to murder someone, then present him with the opportunity to do it and get away with it. The Mastigos has to make him fall head over heels in love with him, only to utterly dash his hopes and tear up his illusions. The Moros comes last, he has to to remind him of his greatest fear, then give him the choice of mastering it or dying. If all three succeed, he awakens, if one fails he doesnt make it and settles as a Sleepwalker forever. The players could use magic to assist, but know that throwing spells directly at his pattern in his current state will screw everything up. They have 12 hours to make this happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Love it, but can't only mages of the same Path see the Mystery Play in question?<br /> <br /> P.S.: We really need SoS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T12:45:07-07:00","id":1085104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/11947-1001-mage-story-hooks?p=1085099#post1085099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Love it, but can't only mages of the same Path see the Mystery Play in question?<br /> <br /> P.S.: We really need SoS.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If it gets in the way of a cool scenario, scrap it. That's my opinion anyway,after all the World of Darkness is full of exceptions to general rules. I think Mages call them Mysteries?<br /> <br /> Totally agree on SoS though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T14:04:48-07:00","id":1085577,"title":"","content":"<b>129)</b> The Consilium/Assembly has always been home to an usually large number of Sleepwalkers. They fill the lower (and even middle) ranks of each Orders' numbers, manage projects, hold Spells, and keep the Awakened world running smoothly. Now, however, there seems to be some kind of virus or infection that is somehow returning them to Sleep. Not only is this horrifying on an existential level, but it jeopardizes the entire power structure as trusted contacts and agents suddenly forget the existence of Magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-29-2017, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T18:47:33-07:00","id":1098634,"title":"","content":"Here's something I wrote with /tg/'s help.<br /> <br /> <b>130)</b> A strange Golem was discovered in the basement of an unpopular Mystagogue who finally passed at the age of 113. <br /> <br /> The Golem is in fact a relic of the Time Before. It is full of faulty, contradictory, incomplete or just outright wrong information, as is typical of pre-Fall relics. It can still teach the Rotes that were used in its creation, and it might have actually accurate insight sometimes. <br /> <br /> However, it is, at the end of the day, a malfunctioning, menial servant. Not a death machine or keeper of great knowledge. <br /> <br /> Conflict over its fate could kick off a storyline. Should it be scrapped or fixed? Can it be scrapped or fixed safely? And for the love of God, can someone keep it away from those damn Sleeper kids?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T00:34:16-07:00","id":1098684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/11947-1001-mage-story-hooks?p=1098634#post1098634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's something I wrote with /tg/'s help.<br /> <br /> <b>130)</b> A strange Golem was discovered in the basement of an unpopular Mystagogue who finally passed at the age of 113.<br /> <br /> The Golem is in fact a relic of the Time Before. It is full of faulty, contradictory, incomplete or just outright wrong information, as is typical of pre-Fall relics. It can still teach the Rotes that were used in its creation, and it might have actually accurate insight sometimes.<br /> <br /> However, it is, at the end of the day, a malfunctioning, menial servant. Not a death machine or keeper of great knowledge.<br /> <br /> Conflict over its fate could kick off a storyline. Should it be scrapped or fixed? Can it be scrapped or fixed safely? And for the love of God, can someone keep it away from those damn Sleeper kids?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> is that how power rangers came to be? all their fight a rasionalisation of their shattered minds eroding under constant memory modifications?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T14:44:14-07:00","id":1098902,"title":"","content":"<b>131</b>) The night of a powerful storm, something momentous happened. The entire area temporarily became a Supernal Verge (to multiple Arcana/Realms, by all accounts) and the more onieromantically inclined members all reported particularly portentous dreams. The next morning, you/the Cabal encounter a Sleeper friend... who is now a Sleepwalker. And registering as an <i>Artifact</i>.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Clarification, if needed. The person is treated much like any other Artifact - Gnosis, Arcana, Powers/Spell Effects, etc. They aren't a Mage so they can't control any of their own Artifact abilities unless they figure out the triggers and trip them though triggers normally. A Mage who is in contact with them, however, can tap any of their Artifact traits normally. So, yes, there might be a scene where they are standing there while Mages argue over who &quot;owns&quot; them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-02-2017, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T09:11:08-07:00","id":1109264,"title":"","content":"<b>132)</b> Irises and Verges to the Invisible Realms and beyond have started appearing in the city, and strange Artifacts and beings emerge from them. At the same time, a legendary Mage who had gone into self-imposed exile returns and reveals a new super Athenaeum. He gathers a meeting of the Orders and receives permission to create a task force of promising Mages from the Mysterium, Arrow and Guardians to collect these strange anomalies and bring them to the new Athenaeum. At the same time, many Seers, Mad, Scelesti and other dangerous Awakened are seeking the anomalies for their own ends, and seem to have developed similar Athenaeums. Whoever gathers the most interesting and powerful anomalies will gain fame and untold rewards.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Gotta Catch 'Em All.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T16:39:55-07:00","id":1110690,"title":"","content":"<b>133)</b> Last night, everything was normal. Then some time this morning, you blacked out and came to with Active Mage Sight on... staring at your own body. A Supernal Being (of your Path) informs you that your current state has been caused by the Ascension attempt of another Mage: now you exist only in the same Supernal/Symbolic state that Mages see when their Mage Sight is Active - a Supernal Ghost, if you will. You will need to find out how this happened, the Mage who caused this, and how to reverse it before the Abyss comes for you. And you can already see the darkened tendrils of unreality creeping in at the edges of your vision...<br /> <br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Other Mages might have been affected too, like your entire Cabal, if needed. Feel free to treat the PCs interchangeably between Mages and Supernal Entities, including Infinite Reach, if so desired. Just be aware of the deadline, and that there is no Summoning Circle your PCs can retreat to.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-02-2017, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T15:34:50-07:00","id":1112966,"title":"","content":"[Sorry this is a bit delayed. And regional - though other nations can adapt it to similar historic events.]<br /> <br /> <b>134)</b> It is the 4th of July, and during a fireworks event, your Peripheral Mage Sight triggered during one particularly spectacular explosion. Your vision even went white. And when it clears, you've found yourself cast back in time to 1776, before the signing of the Declaration of Independence. Why? And how might your action affect the course of history?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T19:15:55-07:00","id":1114361,"title":"","content":"<b>135)</b> While travelling in a large city (Rome, Mumbai, Beijing, Sao Paolo) you hear reports about the rise of tourists being pickpocketed. The strange new crimes involve the victim being hypnotized and willingy handing over their valuables, or withdrawing cash from the nearest ATM. You catch a whiff of magic as you investigate though the pickpockets are in all likeliness mere Sleepers. Who is teaching this new syndicate simple Mind Magic spells, and if so, is this source a threat to the local Consilium?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T04:38:35-08:00","id":1188836,"title":"","content":"<b>136)</b> A prominent scholar of the Mysterium has published their findings: the &quot;random&quot; local magical effects are actually controlled by the network of Ley-Lines and Resonances. And they have even published the &quot;code&quot; of which Resonances, in what order, along which lines, will have what effect. Now there is a territory war for control of key areas to determine which Cabal has control of the Lines they need to achieve the effect they desire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-16-2018, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T08:33:13-08:00","id":1193141,"title":"","content":"[This is actually more an idea for a distinct creature/threat/phenomena, but I can't think of a more fitting thread, and I don't want to make a new one just for this.]<br /> <br /> <b>137)</b> Something has been stalking Sleepwalkers, and even Mages, in the area. It strikes mostly when they are alone, though a few incidents have been caught on surveillance recordings. The victims seem to get attacked by some kind of invisible monster, but scrutiny of the scene with Spirit, Death, and Mind Arcana reveals nothing unexpected for someone attacked and killed. One survivor reported the attack ceasing as soon as they reached a crowded area, but other have been assaulted in small groups. The only commonality is that it appear to avoid Sleepers, leading some Mages to concluded it is Supernal in origin.<br /> <br /> It isn't... <i>quite</i>. It is a spirit-like entity that treats Abyssal presence, such as from Reach and Sleeper observation, like Spirits with the Gauntlet. It mostly operates through Reaching Numina, and as it isn't made of one of the more common types of ephemera nor has stepped into even Twilight, and has thus far escaped detection. The Otherworld it dwells in is neither Shadow, Underworld, or Astral. As for the thing's motives? It may prey upon people, but is generally held at bay by the restrictive nature of its &quot;Gauntlet&quot;. It may actually passively feed upon Supernal magic, and something else turned it against the Awakened in the area. It might be an entirely new creature/phenomena.<br /> <br /> [For those who don't want something completely weird - extra-flavor options:]<br /> <br /> <b>a)</b> The creature may not be Supernal, but its presence <i>is</i>. It is able to manifest from elsewhere due to a persistent spell, which happens to unravel due to the mere presence of Paradox, acting similar to the interference caused by the Gauntlet. Unfortunately, it was the spell of an Archmaster, and it reassembles itself once the disruptive presence is gone. Why would an Archmaster do such a thing, and is there any way to end the spell permanently?<br /> <br /> <b>b)</b> The creature is an <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition/page55\">Achronal</a>... of the Time Before. Paradox didn't exist then, so it loses the Fulcrum Condition it needs to Reach and exert itself whenever Paradox exists. As for why it is attacking Sleepwalkers and the Awakened? Maybe it is a predator from then, acting on timeless (heh) instinct. Maybe it is getting something from those it attacks. Maybe its current existence is pain, and it wants to remove everyone who can see past the lie so that it might finally end, even for a moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-08-2018, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T13:28:03-07:00","id":1196201,"title":"","content":"<b>138)</b> (Either in the PCs area, or one they are visiting) - Mages are spontaneously generating Soul Stones. This doesn't seem to impact their Wisdom, and it hasn't lowered anyone's Gnosis or Willpower, but Mages also don't seem to be able to control it. Random objects they handle seem to become their Soul Stones until their potential Gnosis reaches its current value. This has caused a scavenger hunt of Mages hunting down where their errant Soul Stones may have ended up so they can subsume them and advance (or just limit their Sympathetic vulnerability).<br /> <br /> <b>139)</b> Sleepers in the area have been affected by Nimbus Tilts, and the Consilium/Assembly has asked your Cabal to see what Mage is getting sloppy, or at risk of becoming Mad. But you can't uncover <i>any</i> Mage who is doing it. Everyone affected seems to have passed through one area, though.<br /> <br /> Then <i>it</i> contacts you. The area in question has become a Genius Loci. An <i>Awakened</i> Genius Loci.<br /> <br /> <b>140)</b> Something has happened and converted a number of Sleepwalkers the Cabal knows into living Hallows... and their flesh has transformed into Tass (treat them as having a Hallow rating equal to their Stamina, and Health levels equal to their Mana). Other than various magical side-effects, they are now also being hunted by Manavores and greedy Mages.<br /> <br /> <b>141)</b> A magical phenomena is reverting Sleepwalkers back to Sleepers - at least, adult ones. At the same time, children are becoming Sleepwalkers in large numbers (say 40-90% of all children). Some time around puberty, and definitely by the end of it, they either return to Sleep or Awaken. Considering all the tasks the Awakened community needs done, and the limited number of Mages, the choice is to enlist children in occult tasks or remain under-staffed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-17-2018, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T12:49:13-07:00","id":1196881,"title":"","content":"<b>142)</b> The local ephemeral ecology has been taken over.<br /> <br /> Thyrsus find one Spirit has emerged triumphant over its rivals and now rules as the Spirit Noble of the City. Even it's former superiors can't seem to match it, their every action countered and checked.<br /> <br /> Mastigos have reported odd behavior - Goetia seem to be entering Twilight without any Mages assistance. They are also moving around and urging people toward ideas that don't always correspond to their own nature. And they all report answering to the ideal of the City.<br /> <br /> Moros have observed Ghosts in the area acting with renewed vigor and energy. They are influencing people to restore previously depressed and abandoned areas, and frightening others away from seemingly random locations, animals, and people. They claim to serve the Ghost of the City itself.<br /> <br /> Each would be unusual by themselves, but the truth is stranger still - each representation of the City have joined forces across ephemera into an alliance of regional dominance. How were they even able to do this? And how will it affect existing Mysteries and arrangements?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-04-2018, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T09:15:35-07:00","id":1203038,"title":"","content":"<b>143)</b> Sleepers call it the &quot;Mandela effect&quot;, where you imagine you have seen or heard something but it was false. Of course, sleepers are very good at this specific thing, that's where quiessence shines. The whole phenomenon is meme-worthy popular culture but little more than that.<br /> <br /> Past that, however, there are several cabals who are obsessively hunting for truly worthy Mandela Effects. They theorize that time is constantly being changed, erased and overwritten by powerful beings such as Exarchs or the God-machine for one reason or another, and the Mandela Effect happens when a few people remember things being different and having the different timelines and realities clash in their memories.<br /> <br /> \u200bYour cabal finds something that is a bit off, such as a strangely different version of a famous movie or a history book that details a very different view of history than you were taught in school. Worse still, someone or something wants what you found in order to erase it from existence. Since you were witnesses to it, you are not allowed to go unscathed either and have to fight for survival. Or maybe you are allowed to live, provided you start to work for those time-changers instead.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, you better hope you have your own timelines protected from tampering! If you do not and cannot get it done yourself, better find someone who can...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","user":"Aristarkos","date":". 04-04-2018, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T21:34:35-07:00","id":1203290,"title":"","content":"<b>144)</b> A mage, (preferably a trusted PC) receives an unexpected knock at their door. It's a local Guardian inviting them in for questioning.<br /> <br /> For some reason or other, however, one of the Guardian investigators examined an uninteresting corpse for some unexplained reason and stumbled into a Corpse Mask. The cause of death was Animosity, which shocked the Guardian. This triggered an investigation which uncovered a number of people killed in similar ways and disguised. The only common thread among them, they finally determined, was their strange manner of death, the concealment, and a negative connection to the mage being questioned. Hence the visit.<br /> <br /> Some of the dead were irritants back in grade school and not even thought of since. Further, the mage never did it and never summoned goetia.<br /> <br /> Did something escape from the astral? Did something climb up from below and latch itself to the mage? Is something simply toying with them? Were idle angry words exchanged that are now, somehow, becoming lethal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 04-05-2018, 02:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T08:11:20-07:00","id":1205217,"title":"","content":"<b>145)</b> The children of the PCs (or a family they are close to) are returning from school, talking about their amazing field trips in a manner that clearly speaks more of Magic than even childrens' imagination would account for. What Mystery is this, and has it turned all of the children into Sleepwalkers? Who is so lax in their magic use? The Guardians of the Veil want to know. And there is word that a Seer Pylon involved in education is also investigating the situation.<br /> <br /> Are you ready to sneak aboard the Magic School Bus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-10-2018, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T11:05:37-07:00","id":1205682,"title":"","content":"<b>146)</b> A friend of the PC's is a powerful member of the Adamantine Arrow and has a strong sense of justice. He has spent the better part of the year attempting to root out corruption among the local police force, and has been surprisingly successful at doing so. Now he has disappeared without a trace and the only clue linking to his disappearance is the word &quot;Shield-Bearers&quot;. (Crossover Werewolf)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T19:09:12-07:00","id":1221911,"title":"","content":"147) A serial killer that the news has dubbed the Hangman has become surprisingly active. At first the local Consilium is content to let the local police handle it. Until a body ends up hanging from a lamp post less than a block away from the PC's Sanctum, and another across the street from a frequent meeting place of the Mysterium, and another with &quot;Suffer Not a Witch to Live&quot; Carved into the poor bastard's chest. None of the victims were mages but its clear that the Hangman is trying to send a message to the Mages of the City, but for what purpose?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24168-madman777","name":"Madman777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T18:26:56-07:00","id":1222141,"title":"","content":"148) Broken. Defeated. Humiliated. That's how you left that Seer. Honestly Death would have been kinder. The Seers have decided to retaliate. First they blew up the local Adamantine Arrows to show that even the greatest warriors the Pentacle has to offer die just like anyone else. Next the Local Sliver Ladder the few survivors said that the Seers let them go to give you a warning your next. The Seers have also put out a massive bounty on your heads to every other supernatural in the city promising to let whatever faction does you in rule over the city as the new dominant Species no interference. The offer they made to the Pentacle was slightly different. Turn over the PC's and be rewarded. Hide them and die with them.... or worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24168-madman777","name":"Madman777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T19:42:11-07:00","id":1222568,"title":"","content":"149) Seer Story hook. Congrats you did it! The local Pentacle is all but decimated, and your pylon is top dog among the Seers. You can't sleep. Try as you might each night as you go to bed you have nightmares that make Pandemonium look good by comparison. The question is whose doing it. The local Pentacle is all but gone, and any mage who has the kind of juice to get through your mental defenses you made sure that they died screaming. That doesn't rule out other supernatural beings, but of the ones in town your pylon has always had exceptionally good relations with the ruling vampires, and while you have skinned a few werewolves they sure as hell don't have the ability to do jack shit given the shadow that exists in the wake of the Wizards war you just ended. No one has seen the local Changelings in a couple of years, and the Sin Eaters generally know if they step up they get cut down. The Beasts might be pissed if any of them had family ties, but as far as you know none of them have the power to inflict anything on a mage of your power. Its starting to become a problem you know if the other Seers smell blood in the water you are a dead man. Same with the other supernatural beings. Who is doing this? Why? Better find out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24168-madman777","name":"Madman777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T05:11:03-07:00","id":1229565,"title":"","content":"<b>150) Falling Star</b><br /> One night, Awakened astronomers observed an incoming object, possibly a meteor streaking close to Earth. Until it shifted course and impacted nearby. Checking the news and comparing with Sleeper fellow astronomers, it became clear that it was invisible to those still shrouded by the Lie. You have ventured (or were sent) out to investigate the impact site. The area shows less damage than an object of that size and speed should have inflicted. At the center, buried under the recently fallen impact ejecta you find what can only be described as a ruined space-ship. Bristling with all manner of Supernal energies and items. Is this a remnant of the Time &quot;Before&quot;? Some creation by modern Mages, kept secret somehow? Or is there alien life out there also versed in the Supernal?<br /> <br /> <b>A)</b> Those questions, and deeper investigation, will have to wait. Other forces are also in the area, seeking to claim the secrets and treasures for themselves. (These could be Hunter groups, other supernaturals, Seers, Pentacle Mages if the PCs are Seers, etc.)<br /> <br /> <b>B)</b> Someone else already seems to have gotten here first. The local black market has listed pieces of &quot;alien technology&quot; on auction. There is no telling what havoc letting these magic items fall into the wrong hands may bring.<br /> <br /> <b>C)</b> When you finally find a way to the entrance of the ship, you see tracks leading <i>out</i>. Some are clearly not human. Whatever was in there has escaped, and may now be stalking the area. Or you.<br /> <br /> <b>D)</b> When you manage to breach the hull and gain entry, you find a message, scrawled in High Speech: <i>&quot;They are coming!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>E)</b> While most of the ship is ruined, <i>some</i> parts are obviously still functional. Like the intruder detection and countermeasures, which have now activated and are very much trying to kill and/or keep you imprisoned.<br /> <br /> [I'm sure more people can some up with additional hooks, variant details/backstory, etc. I'm just going to stop here to prevent bloat, and to work on some of the devices that might be aboard.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T03:56:36-07:00","id":1240788,"title":"","content":"151) What's my name again?<br /> <br /> A new mage ( possibly one of the players) Attempts to use their sympathetic name as a yantra to cast a spell only to find it fails. The reason being that it isn't their real sympathetic name. This is not unheared of in cases of adoptions or foundlings (see sidebar on page 172 for why). Sometimes a child is abandoned after they acquire their sympathetic name and grow up thinking of themselves by a different one. The problem here is that it is proving almost impossible to find out what their real sympathetic name is as a result. Records either don't exist or claim the child's birth name to be what they previously thought it was. Time magic fails to locate the person earlier then their adoption.<br /> Not knowing their own sympathetic name could be an added protection. But the fact remains that something is shrouding their origins. Who or what is responsible? Do they seek their own name out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13691-margul","name":"Margul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T06:34:06-07:00","id":1242929,"title":"","content":"<b>152)</b> Something has been going on in the area - spells almost feel as if they want to escape their casters, being automatically Relinquished (Unsafely) without cost, unless the Mage spends a Willpower point to keep them under their Spell Control. The local Mysterium is claiming this is proof that Magic Is Alive. The local Guardians of the Veil are apoplectic at the dangers this causes. Other Mages are merely annoyed that it feels like their spell casting is being taxed. There seems to be no other consequences beyond the automatic Relinquishment - spells still expire and decay as they normally do. Few Mages bother at longer Durations than a few days, so long term decay effects aren't thoroughly studied.<br /> <br /> But what exactly is happening and what could be causing it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T10:14:11-07:00","id":1244541,"title":"","content":"<b>153)</b> [Seer or incautious Mage only] <b>You Must <s>Construct</s> Recruit Additional Pylons</b><br /> You have been struck by a wave of dreams, visions, and Mystery Commands. An Exarch is commanding you to step up Seer recruitment in the area and is &quot;encouraging&quot; you to monitor certain people who may Awaken soon, and bring them together into a new Pylon. You've even &quot;found&quot; an Artifact to aid in this... when you next returned to your Sanctum (if if you don't already have one, you &quot;stumble&quot; across one sometime soon).<br /> <br /> (optional additions)<br /> <b>A)</b> [Non-Seer only] Except you aren't a Seer and you don't worship the Exarchs. So why did one of them pick you? How do you tell &quot;no&quot; to a Supernal Mage-God that can find you anywhere and seems very interested in you, specifically, doing this thing?<br /> <b>B)</b> [Seer only] Except, by all that you can figure out, this Exarch is <i>one from a different Ministry</i>. Why has a rival chosen you? How would your own master or peers react if they found out? Are you able to plead &quot;conflicts of interest&quot;?<br /> <b>C)</b> The Exarch seems to be a <i>new</i> one (for what that is worth to timeless Supernal Mage-Gods), and recruiting Pylons is the first step in their new Ministry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T00:04:29-07:00","id":1244741,"title":"","content":"154) Cell phones all over the area start to register as Mysteries -- big ones! Turns out a popular guided meditation app is loaded with Supernal messages. Is it a scheme to encourage mass Awakenings, or is the app's developer in the middle of their own mystery play? Or is there something else far darker at work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T04:36:38-07:00","id":1381269,"title":"","content":"155) There's a new Proximi line in the world. Connected to the Sixth Watchtower, members of this line need to kill a willworker every so often or they suffer from agonizing pain. Thankfully the pain doesn't actually prevent them from doing anything, technically, but that's not really a positive thing when you're the only willworker in sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T04:37:26-07:00","id":1381270,"title":"","content":"156) A semi-lupine, Abyssal monster by the name of Fenrir drifts into town.<br /> The monster has a deep unending hunger for the flesh of the Awakened, &amp; is completely invisible to Arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T04:38:05-07:00","id":1381271,"title":"","content":"157) A powerful willworker managed to open a direct portal to the Supernal Realms, flooding the area with Supernal energies. The willworker is now dead, crushed by the pressure of the portal &amp; overwhelmed by the huge amount of Supernal energies.<br /> Unfortunately, we can't take a breather just yet. Whilst the portal was open several creatures of the Supernal Realms came through &amp; many of them didn't return home.<br /> Something weird about the portal has ensured that the creatures aren't finding the local atmosphere to be toxic, but this still isn't their home.<br /> Hunt them all down &amp; return them to the heavens from whence they came.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T04:38:52-07:00","id":1381272,"title":"","content":"158) For the last month there has been a vast, open hole to the Abyss sitting in the sky, visible to all including mundane society.<br /> Just yesterday, Abyssal phenomena started to skyrocket. Gulmoths, acamoths, Scelesti &amp; all sorts of other threats from the Abyss are being encountered right across the length &amp; breadth of the city. The Red Word has started to perform their rituals right out in the open.<br /> What was with the delay? How are we expected to combat so many Abyssal threats at once? What made the hole? And how are we supposed to end this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T04:39:57-07:00","id":1381274,"title":"","content":"159) A willworker skilled in Time Arcana has come to the conclusion that the Mayans were right. The end of the world was scheduled to happen at the end of 2012.<br /> But something interfered with the scheduled apocalypse &amp; now all these disasters including the appearance of ISIS, Donald Trump getting elected, &amp; the coronavirus crisis are all the result of the world lasting for longer than it was supposed to.<br /> The willworker has decided to fix this. They will go back to the appointed time &amp; make sure the world ends as it was scheduled to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T04:40:43-07:00","id":1381275,"title":"","content":"160) The Hierarch has started listening to what they believe to be a goetic spirit that they summoned, but is actually a demon of pride from Inferno.<br /> It has managed bind itself to the Hierarch's very magic, rendering it nearly impossible to exorcise as it can draw up the magic to guard itself against any attempt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T04:42:24-07:00","id":1381276,"title":"","content":"161) You've found a small, yet growing town in the middle of a desert where a sizable number of the population is Abyssal Conceptions, across all the generations.<br /> Complicating any decision you might make is the fact that any mother of an Abyssal Conception in the area is free from the madness that normally comes with their situation.<br /> And haven't you got a female relative, in the first/second/third trimester giving off faint Abyssal readings, who claims to be a virgin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T04:43:04-07:00","id":1381277,"title":"","content":"162) There's a false demesne of the Sixth Watchtower growing in an important government building (police station, prison, city hall, etc.).<br /> Readings indicate that something is preventing it from self-destructing by itself. Someone's going to have to go in &amp; force it to collapse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T04:43:53-07:00","id":1381278,"title":"","content":"163) There's a false demesne in a nearby petstore/florists/gardening shop/the woods.<br /> A group of willworkers identify its presence &amp; set out to shut it down. A pack of werewolves found it first. They have misinterpreted the nature of the place &amp; have claimed it for the essence that just seeps out of the walls &amp; floor.<br /> The wolves have no intention of letting the willworkers shut it down &amp; don't believe them when they tell of the lifecycle of a false demesne.<br /> You've got to, somehow, get past the super-charged wolves &amp; shut this thing down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T04:44:25-07:00","id":1381279,"title":"","content":"164) Mages have started using mythological &amp; famous historical names as shadow names, with far greater frequency.<br /> Examples include: Joan d'Arc, Odin, Tyr, Fenrir, Achilles, Arthur Pendragon, Lancelot, Napoleon Bonaparte, &amp; many others.<br /> But there are consequences to using names like these, which are starting to pile up.<br /> Lancelot has entered into a relationship with their best friend's spouse, Arthur Pendragon. Fenrir has developed an insatiable hunger. Tyr has lost a hand in the process of trapping Fenrir. Napoleon Bonaparte has started a revolution.<br /> What's up with this new trend? And how can it be stopped before something really bad happens?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T18:35:34-07:00","id":1381497,"title":"","content":"165)Long ago, an archmaster catastrophically failed casting an Imperial Time spell, and the resulting Paradox causes him to enter Twilight as a powerless observer, unable to even communicate, only to Materialize for one day and one night (NOT necessarily contiguous) every hundred years, <br /> <br /> Now, six hundred years after his catastrophic mistake, the archmaster is set to Materialize once more---and is <i>desperate</i> end this eternal hell, no matter the cost!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T18:50:35-07:00","id":1384331,"title":"","content":"166) There are constant protests happening just outside your new startup business. It's making things difficult. Several potential employees have been injured or have just decided not to brave the madness for work.<br /> The protests appear to be being organized by some hippies who accuse of being a witch you tortures Mother Earth.<br /> What does that mean, &amp; how can you get rid off them?<br /> \u25cf Uses the Keepers of the Source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T18:51:07-07:00","id":1384332,"title":"","content":"167) The Promethean Brotherhood's experiments into figuring out how to make the Rite of Hecate work, have yielded a terrible monster.<br /> A creature with the appearance of human &amp; the power to devour Arcana, it relentlessly hunts &amp; slaughters any mage it comes across.<br /> It's seem you &amp; now you find a way to kill, if not for the lives of every other mage in the area, then for yourself.<br /> \u25cf Uses the Promethean Brotherhood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T21:35:21-07:00","id":1384351,"title":"","content":"168) The tectonic plaques are rapidly shifting and with them countries drift and separate, akin to ships. The booms of Hallows being created and destroyed are throwing the supernatural into disarray. Amid this chaos, Sleeper minds grapple to separate &quot;real knowledge&quot; from the &quot;fakes that seem to crowd all references&quot;. Someone is behind this, but who or what has the power to rearrange the very pillars of the Earth ?<br /> <br /> 169) (Inspired by Don't Rest Your Head) Sometimes mortals go on too long without sleep and then they see a gateway to a city of nightmares. The poor fools that step through enter its Astral realm, where they gain Numina, Influences and apply dream logic to stats. Greater power can be gained by damaging one's sanity. Those caught asleep by the nightmares risk becoming them. Now that they crossed the threshold, the nightmares can also cross back to capture them. Knowing this, how do you plan to rescue them ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 04-28-2020, 08:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T14:48:11-07:00","id":1385306,"title":"","content":"170) The Consilia is in an uproar, its walls are covered by 20 High Speech banners of pure prime energy, each bearing a heraldric symbol. In the center, you see a lunargent lance stabbed into the ground, bearing a crest spelling in High Speech: Seneschal of the Nethermoon. Who are they and what do they want ?<br /> <br /> 171) Sometimes you can see ectoplasm falling in the drops of rain. If enough accumulates in a pool or puddle of water, anything inside it sinks into Death Twilight. What exactly is infusing the clouds with this power ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-02-2020, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T03:03:01-07:00","id":1395559,"title":"","content":"172) A Free Council Arcanthus discovers a Grimoire which in horrific explicit detail tells a cautionary tale about a Silver Ladder Arcanthus arrogant enough to attempt to summon and bind a particularly nasty Gentry of the Fair Folk known for their cannibalistic appetites, and how he received a boon along with a letter describing what what he going to ask for without even having to bother casting the spell but then all the terrible things which ended up happening to the mage including having to feed the creature both of his legs, an eye and his right arm in magically resistant wounds or lose even more people he cared about. There is a dire warning against attempting to use Fate to summon and Bind one of the Gentry of the Fair Folk. After the warning is the spell and True Name of that True Fae. Of course the Free Council Arcanthus scoffs, because she believes she knows where the Silver Ladder went astray. Obviously he shouldn't have been trying to use the True Fae for corrupt presumably self serving ends, shouldn't have chosen such a cruel and wicked monster, and should have completed the summoning and binding instead of just accepting the preemptive Trojan-horse gift. Satisfied at her own cleverness and feeling quite superior to the previous owner of the Grimoire she research a wee spritely Gentry with a reputation for loving fun and freedom as it gallivants on gossamer wings which would surely want to help her in the goal of stopping the Seers of the Throne from bulldozing a Homeless encampment and city green space so they could build yet another skyscaper to overlay aerial Hallow with a greedy corporate board room to monopolize the mana and turn even more of the city's resonance to oppressive greed. Secure that she's chosen the right True Fae and that with noble intentions surely such a freedom loving being would work with her willingly.<br /> <br /> She is ready to cast the spell, going to go through with it no matter what... and right before she begins <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1395547-2e-mystery-note-from-the-future-in-the-present#post1395547\">a magical note from the future appears</a>... just like one did for that arrogant foolish Silver ladder... it explains how she now has allies at the city council whom will listen to her in order to prevent the seers of the throne from inflicting more tyranny or building a tower. Then she reads the last line and her blood turns cold. Just like the grimoire describes the ending the note the Silver Ladder had the same ominous &quot;careful what you wish for...&quot;. Taking a break an realizing she still has all the prep to cast the spell she relaxes and focuses. She'll just summon and bind the Fae to see what is going on, that's one of the places the Silver Ladder messed up and she wasn't at all like him, she thinks to herself. But The summoning does NOTHING, she feels Fate completely ignoring her pushes and pulls. She begins really looking at note with her Mage sight and what she sees deeply bothers her as the Note is a Mystery and even the surface isn't good news. Before Delving any deeper she phones a group of friends to come over and help her sort this all out and investigate the mysterious note from the future and the curse its warning conveys.<br /> <br /> And the PCs are whom she calls. I mean odds are the PC know an idealistic Free Council Arcanthus whom is an activist for the down trodden and against corporate Seers of the Throne, if not then introducing someone like that who is affable in one story and then starting this story after a couple other stories is a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T19:48:03-07:00","id":1397206,"title":"","content":"The neighborhood kids have taken to talking about some crazy stuff. It takes a while, but eventually, mages catch wind and hear about the ritual that supposedly grants wishes. There is a list of rules to it all, from when to where, to how and, most importantly what can be wished for. A sacrifice must be made and either something of similar value is brought in or something is excised.<br /> <br /> Fate magi that hear the details are surprised to realize how much of this is accurate. Accurate enough that it's suspicious. <br /> Is someone teaching mysteries? Has a Sleepwalker found a grimoire? Could there be a Ananke in play? Could there be a being of some other sort editing fates?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T21:41:13-07:00","id":1397227,"title":"","content":"174) The building went up in flames, yet everything was frozen rather than charred. The people trapped inside died of hypothermia, their skin fully necrosed, their heartbeats halted. Yet hours later they awoke in the morgue, healthy, lucid, confused....and changed.<br /> <br /> <b>Answer:</b> A minor Ministry of the Psychopomp harnessed The Abyssal Maw, an Artifact that consumes part of the user's soul to shoot Stygian fire. This bale blaze sends victims' souls to be tortured in Cocytos, in the Underworld domain of Gehenna, while their bodies are Possesed by its inhabitants. Now that the tests are done, they will attempt to target gatherings of Pentacle mages. They seek to profit from planting traitors, revel in the torment of their prisoners and capture the Exarch's favor before the Maw's price becomes too dear to pay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-18-2020, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T11:43:17-07:00","id":1399340,"title":"","content":"175.<b>Ki-En-Gir</b><br /> A great victory over a Scelestus archmage has occurred, truly a victory for Supernal Truth! But now comes the TRULY difficult part: sifting through the lore and magical items assembled over nearly a century of Awakened life by an Aswadim. Much of this lore is tainted, but enough of it is salvageable that it bears careful cautious investigation.<br /> <br /> The story of the origins of Sumeria are supposedly revealed, of s land the Scelesti called Ki-En-Gir, a kingdom of blasphemies where worship of the Abyss stood supreme and antinomian sorcery was first learnt.<br /> <br /> Apparently, some other culture---a rival empire of some sort---laid Ki-En-Gir low, and, from the ashes arose Sumeria.<br /> <br /> The dead Aswadim had the belief it was the Exarchs who demolished Ki-En-Gir, as he could find no information whatsoever of Ki-En-Gir's destroyer, other than that they were led by priests who were also gods.<br /> <br /> Several locations were identified by the Aswadim as being temples containing Abyssal lore. Most of these places have been plundered, but one has not.<br /> <br /> The players get sent it to explore this ruin and brave its dangers. What horrors await them in the Middle East? What buried torments of Ki-En-Gir will they encounter? And what of this mysterious rival empire that seems to have wiped from the memory of Sleeper historians? Was this other empire from the Time Before, or were they slaves of the Exarchs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 06-27-2020, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T10:38:30-07:00","id":1399617,"title":"","content":"176.<b>The Well</b><br /> A mage buys an old, dilapidated mansion with the intent of turning it into a Sanctum loaded with magical features...and, a week into the mundane side of the remodeling, he finds a well in the basement that seems to be infinitely deep.<br /> At first fearing it an Avernian Gate or a Schism, the well leads...nowhere. It just keeps going down, into the dark, without end.<br /> A week later, the mage, using Sleeper climbing gear, a winch and his mastery of Matter magic, plunges into the well's deeps. He then...vanishes.<br /> Unfortunately, the Hierarch has become Obsessed with this Mystery and swiftly followed suit. Now the players must delve down in to rescue the Hierarch. As they plunge ever further downwards, they realize they're somewhere strange quickly after hitting the 50-mile-deep mark. The well shaft grows cold, and faces seem to appear in the rime. They're still impossibly in the material Realm, however.<br /> Do they keep going deeper, hoping to find their missing Hierarch? Is there even an end to the well shaft? If so, what's down there? Who dug the well, in the first place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T00:20:59-07:00","id":1399748,"title":"","content":"Winter in the hills of Keenalee see a strange visitor: Winter's Tear. The creature steals an animal from each field until it finds a building with a boiled custard sitting under a holly branch. After finding that, it sets a blessing on the building and its owner. (it has some odd rules about how it interprets that.) In either case, it leaves a centered fox print in muddy snow. It leaves no tracks, otherwise.<br /> <br /> It only comes out at sunset after the first snow and the first rain that follows it before the equinox; it doesn't show up every year. Apparently, there are other possible conditions, which is why the region tends to put out the &quot;winter custard&quot; and visit each other as part of their winter festivities. It's safe to drink all the custard after twilight ends. The path it follows is extremely unpredictable. <br /> <br /> The locals are actually not generally aware of the legends anymore. The incidents of strange animal disappearances has increased as locals stopped being as fond of the festival, but the number of people still practicing is high enough that the incidence is pretty low.<br /> <br /> The Conciluim governing that mystery only has a few elderly mages.<br /> <br /> One of these became extremely agitated and called out to their outside allies to help find his friend. He believes that Winter's Tear took him in an unprecedented attack on a human. The signs are there.<br /> <br /> Perhaps he got too close? Where could it have ever gone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 06-29-2020, 03:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T18:39:23-07:00","id":1400229,"title":"","content":"178.<b>The Corpse Husband</b><br /> A Moros alchemist in [Fill-In-The-Blank] has summoned what he thought was a Shade of Stygia, to resurrect his dead Sleepwalker lover. The summoning apparently works, and the two men are reunited...<br /> <br /> ...except that they AREN'T. He did not do his research properly, and reached into the Underworld, instead, and dredged up a shapeshifting horror that was born undead in some unimaginably distant epoch. This creature hides among its prey, feeding on human flesh when possible. If it does not kill every single day, it will fall back into the Underworld. It does not wish this.<br /> <br /> The bodies are beginning to pile up. The Consilium is convinced a Tremere is involved. The players are ordered by the Hierarch to investigate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T13:55:21-07:00","id":1400390,"title":"","content":"In 1913, following the publication of Wegener's continental drift theory, mages joined into that debate. As expected, many free Council members were in the thick of it challenging or supporting the research. For years, it was assumed that the errors of the early mage researchers were largely errors of methodology or records that paralleled the Sleepers' own..<br /> <br /> Recently, in one of the Assembly Archives, it was discovered that one of the more obsessed FC of that era had gone farther than most knew. His cabal went so far as to create a legacy devoted to measuring and mapping large scale geological features. Their methods were supernaturally precise and they verified with solid mundane methods. (albeit much less accurate) Their maps were extremely precise and performing two independent surveys was their standard approach. When something was particularly important, they used five.<br /> <br /> Something they found lead to them quietly walking away from the Free Assemblies, research nearly complete, in 1961. The controversy surrounding their research fades quickly. The Councilium handling the question of continents essentially shuttered completely in 1968. <br /> <br /> The recent researchers, having investigated the methods, cannot account for the level of error in the maps with the level of rigor their cartographers applied. Perhaps some of the mages still live. What does it say if most of the team left the FC for the Guardians or Mysterium? Were the maps falsified or could things have dramatically changed? What happened to the legacy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T12:29:21-07:00","id":1401166,"title":"","content":"<b>180)</b> A preacher in the streets has been claiming that the Neptunians will come destroy the city in a 3 day event known as The Flood, to take place in World Oceans Day. She founded a cult called the Friends of Neptune, saying they tasked her to pick 100 worthy souls to be saved. These chosen are promised to live on Neptune in New Atlantis, with every luxury existent and many comforts beyond imagination. <br /> <br /> The Consilia would normally dismiss her as a charlatan, but she seems to have supernatural powers that resemble magitek and many claim that she opened portals beyond the Cerulean Gate, corridors to journey to distant mystic areas of the cosmos. Where did these Sleepers get this knowledge and how does it defy the Quiescence ? What if the Flood is real ? Can the city even be saved or must it be evacuated before its too late ?<br /> <br /> Better get answers soon, the government has sent special agents to investigate.<br /> <br /> <b>Answer:</b> Its a Changeling Loyalist to an Alien Abduction style True Fae, the city's Lost have long infiltrated Task Force Valkyrie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-05-2020, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T06:12:18-07:00","id":1408902,"title":"","content":"<b>181)</b> You remember clearly the disbelieving tears of joy on their faces as they saw the portal had lead their archeomancer cabal back to reality, together with the shock of everyone upon seeing an Abyssal Iris temporarily open in the middle of the Consilia's meeting. <br /> <br /> The Mysterium's most sacred rituals have removed the bulk of the taint, but they can expect to spend the next few years under a Libertine therapist, and at least the next decade under Guardian observation. Still, they told an unbelievable tale even as their frayed sanity made you question the clarity of the memories.<br /> <br /> Apparently one of the great sages of the Awakened City predicted the Abyss' incursion upon the Fallen as a possibility and that it could be leverages by those mad or desperate enough to cause untold suffering. In order to prevent this, she created a device that could repurpose the most fearsome spirits, the Idigam, into the perfect predators to devour the Abyss.<br /> <br /> She broke the device and hid its parts within the Celestial Ladder, ensuring that when it collapsed, its pieces would be sent to the Void, ensuring their survival past any temporal revisions.<br /> <br /> The notes, debriefs and those who compiled them are still being monitored for signs of Abyssal taint. In the meantime, the Hierarch was able to reveal that many more quest for the pieces. Apart from veteran Scelestus, there were also Seers that navigate the Outer Nothingness by wielding limited authority over some denizens, an army of clockwork parascientific automatons and even pilgrims wielding a sacred flame. What happened to them is unclear, its enough of a miracle the expedition made it back, doubtlessly due to being composed of very experienced masters.<br /> <br /> Why didn't the Atlanteans activate the device immediately? Why are those other parties questing for it ? There is no time to be idle, the race has already begun and the greatest prize awaits those that can snatch it from the maws of madness itself.<br /> <br /> <b>Observation:</b> While the journey is supposed to be a &quot;suicidally insane&quot; quest for a highly powerful cabal, nothing says they initially need to know about it. Their initial experiences could be researching, gathering the materials to help experienced masters prepare and dealing with the fallout of the expeditions themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-18-2020, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T08:51:01-07:00","id":1414209,"title":"","content":"<b>182. The Book of Days</b><br /> A local Mysterium cabal found a mysterious book, named &quot;O Livro dos Dias&quot; (transl. &quot;The Book of Days&quot;). The book has a preface, a few written pages and several blank pages. The author - a mage named Taowbeh - explains in the preface that the book is capable to predict future Awakenings.<br /> In the few written pages there is the detailed description of the events that culminated in the Awakening of the characters. There's also the description of an Awakening that will happen in the next few days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Swing on the spiral of our divinity and still be a human&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":25961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25961-redzone","user":"Redzone","date":". 09-18-2020, 01:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25961-redzone","name":"Redzone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T10:54:57-07:00","id":1414425,"title":"","content":"<b>183. The pie shop</b><br /> A nameless order opens a pie shop in the Astral. They sell pies that contains psychic impressions of random sleepers memories. A character tries one of the pies and is surprised by a memory of his childhood seen through the eyes of another person; the psychic impression contains details that the character had never noticed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Swing on the spiral of our divinity and still be a human&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25961-redzone","name":"Redzone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T13:20:34-07:00","id":1414457,"title":"","content":"<b>184.</b> The new Rhadamantian Minister was just appointed, but he isn't a mage. From February 13th to 15th, a werewolf was given a crown of Underworld metals and wailing souls during a corrupted version of Lupercalia. <br /> <br /> In the wake of this profane ceremony, an army of ghosts emerged from a new Domain, the Aventine Hill. The new Minister claims to be Remus, favored son of Sheppard Wolf (I imagine her personality to be like Granny Goodness), who brokered a deal to reclaim what was taken from her favored child. Six Strixes lead his armies, some ghosts posses the recently deceased to reclaim the city. A few bear masks and seek to &quot;recall wayward citizens back to the Hill&quot;. A new Mystery Cult of Remus has sprung up, killings have increased and mad cultists speak of a great ritual.<br /> <br /> What deal did the Seers broker with the ancient spirit ? Is the new Minister truly Remus ? We can worry about that later, 12 Stryxes have contacted mages all over the city with a dire warning: the reincarnation of Romulus must be found.<br /> <br /> <i>Observation:</i> The crown on Lupercalia is a stealthy reference to Julius Caesar, this is a misdirection gambit on his part to get the cabal to fulfill the real terms of the deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 09-18-2020, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T22:22:46-07:00","id":1416571,"title":"","content":"Here is one inspired by Mushishi (that series has the potential for so many interesting Mysteries)<br /> <br /> <b>185)</b> Hundreds of years ago, this city was dying. Its soil barren, its ley lines pulsing with woeful Resonance, even Hallows had become rare and weak. Then a master summoned down an item from Arcadia, one that was a boon and an Artifact, a promising future and a heartbreaking doom.<br /> <br /> The Artifact was a seed, the color of a grain of wheat, but shaped like a dog's fang. Planting it at a Hallow would cause it to dissolve into the ley lines, to infuse itself into the city. Its Resonance would improve, Hallows would grow more powerful and plentiful, even Sleepers would be visited by prosperity. The effect would eventually fade, but by then the movement towards harmony was very powerful.<br /> <br /> There was, however, a price to pay. The seed would eventually sprout out of the weakest mage in the city. It would grow on their mouth like a tooth, consuming their life force, eventually killing them and becoming ready for use once more.<br /> <br /> Our predecessors reluctantly used it and upon that sacrifice they laid the foundations of the city as we know today. But once the deed was done, they sealed it away.<br /> <br /> But recently someone stole it. We need you to get it back. We will show you where it was held. But you cannot tell a single soul about this task. Many desperate Awakened will start warring for Hallows and poisoning others, desperately trying to prevent themselves from being picked. <br /> <br /> Furthermore, many spirits vanished the last time the seed was used, so many spirits, including the current City Father, would quickly escalate their actions to save themselves. Were they to hear a whisper of this, it could cause a war, or even have familiars turn on their partners. The actions we all had to take to contain the chaos and deal with the werewolves were.....shameful (its not clear if they mean diplomatic or combat). <br /> <br /> There is a reason I (the Hierarch) called this cabal and not the Councilors. The simultaneous emergence of so many Hallows and altering of ley lines created chaos for the Guardians and Arrows for decades. It would be best if this was handled by those without the connections to take....harsh...action.<br /> <br /> Find the seed, prevent it from being planted and return it to us and you will gain a major boon. Refuse and we will simply wipe this conversation from your minds. What do you choose ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-06-2020, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T16:37:57-07:00","id":1418734,"title":"","content":"<b>186)</b> There is a giant metal ship in the sky, the size of a continent. Atlantean runes cover it, but the technology looks to be from another world. But its human somehow, halfway between an archaic cathedral of coral and a futuristic human space colony.<br /> <br /> The thing is, records say its always been there since pre-history. Sleepers acknowledge it as part of the landscape, but no one has actually found a way to get inside. Where did this thing come from, how do you enter it and what secret does it hold ?<br /> <br /> <b>187)</b> The latest operation of the Awakening Gambit bore unusual results. The subject did Awaken in a near death experience. In addition, a ghost was produced, but this is not unheard of for such matters.<br /> <br /> The odd part is that is was Metamorphic, mingling the histories and natures of the subject and the newly created ghost on a fundamental level. This has resulted in a Sleepwalker wielding ephemeral powers of death, anchored to an Awakened ghost.<br /> <br /> Their past is constantly being altered as key elements and places phase in and out of existence, leaving echoes that can be temporarily summoned and stabilized via Time magic. Normally, the connection to the Watchtower would stabilize their timeline just enough and that is effectively what is happening, as it constantly attempts to sort it all out.Yet it cannot, because their shared past has a tear, a gash, a wound that was clawed out and cannot be healed. Someone interfered and took a piece of their history right as they Awakened, but who did it, how did they hide themselves from the Gambit and their cabal. Most importantly, what are they using the pilfered past for ?<br /> <br /> <b>188)</b> An old vineyard has just shut down with the recent passing of an aged master. Some vintages contain tass, organically grown by enhanced grapes, producing exquisite flavors as Resonances were combined. Some caskets use water from the Hedge infused with the roots of thunder. There is a summoning room keyed to all things culinary and drink related. But the most spectacular thing of them all is a golem, powered by the master's soul stone. Per his last written request and ratified by the Lex Magicka, the cabal has inherited his estate, provided they also take on his debt, completing a peculiar bit of research for a vampiric patron.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-18-2020, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T15:40:29-08:00","id":1421352,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I removed 78 of the original post. Holocaust denial is not a valid adventure hook.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T15:24:08-08:00","id":1422829,"title":"","content":"One inspired a bit by xianxia, masking an Abyssal patron<br /> <br /> <b>189) </b> Mages aren't the only ones who seek immortality, sometimes mortal occultist become obsessed with it. Some witness the Supernal in their quest. Others succeed, becoming something more than human, at a terrible price. Most tend to die before managing it, but some are too stubborn to stop even then.<br /> <br /> What makes this unusual is that there are two of them acting in unison, the ghost of an obsessive seeker and a Sleepwalker researcher. The ghost has been sustaining him through his anchor: a tome made of perfected flesh of various beings, merged together by some guttural hexing, mystically stitched together with a Frankenstein patchwork of curses. It sustains the follower as they travel to decypher its formula for the elixir.<br /> <br /> So far we knew him as a harmless store clerk, a useful provider of magical materials in a small occult shop. Lately he claimed to have made real progress, even approximating simple magical effects using a litany of runes and mantras. But the runes look like melodies from a guzheng and the mantras taste like hermium. He mentioned something about the next steps requiding some lost cauldrons for concocting medicine. That is all I know, I just gave you some very valuable information, so consider my boon paid in full.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 11-10-2020, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-22T14:02:45-08:00","id":1429561,"title":"","content":"<b>190)</b> No doubt recent event have been unnerving. Mages with mangled Gnosis, bartering away their potential via soul stones or being blackmailed into it by others, both heedless in chasing their Obsessions.<br /> <br /> The almost viral emergence of more Rapt in the city, from both the Pentacle and the Seers. People are too tempted to chase their Obsessions harder, a convenient insight or limited time opportunity appears all to often, tempting them to go over the edge.<br /> <br /> Some clues point you at a mage trying to collect soul stones, trying to remake this city as a Demesne of all 10 Arcana. In contrast, some suggest this is the work of a Banisher, seeking to cast out the Supernal from the city with a perfect Annulity. A few clues point to a Scelestus, whether one seeking to use the Annulity to free a bound Gulmoth, dessecrate the souls stones to facilitate the passage of an Intruder or both is still a matter of debate.<br /> <br /> I am here to tell you, those are all true. You face not one puppet master but 3, competing with each other from the shadows. They are at a stalemate, a deadlock. My mentor, the Pentacle/Seer mage, is getting close to Rapture. <br /> <br /> Had things progressed as they did, she would have broken, it was an inevitable consequence of their situation. But then you lot happened, you imbalanced the equation ever so slightly and its there I see hope, for this city and for her. <br /> <br /> All of them saw you as a risk, one tried to eliminate you so far. But I spirited you away in the last moment. They don't you or I are alive, we can use that to our advantage. Much needs to be done, lets get started.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T06:51:06-08:00","id":1429742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/11947-1001-mage-story-hooks?p=1429561#post1429561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>190)</b> No doubt recent event have been unnerving. Mages with mangled Gnosis, bartering away their potential via soul stones or being blackmailed into it by others, both heedless in chasing their Obsessions.<br /> <br /> The almost viral emergence of more Rapt in the city, from both the Pentacle and the Seers. People are too tempted to chase their Obsessions harder, a convenient insight or limited time opportunity appears all to often, tempting them to go over the edge.<br /> <br /> Some clues point you at a mage trying to collect soul stones, trying to remake this city as a Demesne of all 10 Arcana. In contrast, some suggest this is the work of a Banisher, seeking to cast out the Supernal from the city with a perfect Annulity. A few clues point to a Scelestus, whether one seeking to use the Annulity to free a bound Gulmoth, dessecrate the souls stones to facilitate the passage of an Intruder or both is still a matter of debate.<br /> <br /> I am here to tell you, those are all true. You face not one puppet master but 3, competing with each other from the shadows. They are at a stalemate, a deadlock. My mentor, the Pentacle/Seer mage, is getting close to Rapture.<br /> <br /> Had things progressed as they did, she would have broken, it was an inevitable consequence of their situation. But then you lot happened, you imbalanced the equation ever so slightly and its there I see hope, for this city and for her.<br /> <br /> All of them saw you as a risk, one tried to eliminate you so far. But I spirited you away in the last moment. They don't you or I are alive, we can use that to our advantage. Much needs to be done, lets get started.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm a little confused. Could you please explain this plot hook in greater OOC detail?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T08:28:47-08:00","id":1429747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/11947-1001-mage-story-hooks?p=1429742#post1429742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm a little confused. Could you please explain this plot hook in greater OOC detail?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure thing. There are 3 mages that wish to collect a set of Soul stones from all 10 Arcana, each for different reasons. The Pentacle/Seer mage wants to make a Demesne of all 10 Arcana, making an area free from the Lie for their own purposes. The Banisher wants to make an Annulity of all Arcana, isolating an area from the Supernal. The Scelestus wants to befoul them to summon an Invader or awaken a bound Gulmoth under the city. All have done research on the rituals and resources needed to do this.<br /> <br /> The catch is that only Rapt produce soul stones that are not of the Inferior Arcana of the Paths, and even then only for Arcana related to their Fault. So the 3 are manipulating all mages in the Consilia from the shadows, making it too easy to become Rapt. Obsessions become more tempting, breakthroughs or limited windows of opportunity appear more often to drive mages away from Wisdom. All the while they try to gather as many soul stones as possible via black market deals. <br /> <br /> But somehow they are at cross purposes (maybe their rituals are mutually exclusive), each manipuling catspaws to get in the way of the other. Essentially they are in a deadlock. The escalation is driving the Pentacle/Seer mage ever closer to Rapture. <br /> <br /> The cabal are at the crossfires of this as they investigate the Mystery. They disturb the power balance. Eventually one of the 3 lures them to a deathtrap. But the Pentacle/Seer mage's apprentice saves them, faking their death, asking for help to end the madness and save their mentor. Now the cabal can engage in their own secret missions, to take the offensive to neutralize the 3 threats and save the sanity of the Consilium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 12-25-2020, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-15T10:13:49-08:00","id":1432324,"title":"","content":"191) 30 years ago, the city was struck by a magical storm that killed all of the Awakened. All magical attempts to find out what happened fail. Temporal scrying reveals nothing, like that time never existed. However, recently an old Grimoire has been found, rumored to belong to a Wise one who lived before the catastrophe. In the tome, there is also a photo, with an unusual note on its back, written as if by a madman:<br /> &quot;HE IS COMING! WE CAN NO LONGER ESCAPE HIM, FOR HE CAN FOLLOW US EVERYWHERE! THE ONLY SAFE PLACE IS IN THE MIND! FORGIVE ME, JAMAL, BUT THIS IS THE ONLY WAY TO ENSURE SOMEONE DEFEATS HIM!&quot;<br /> The photo shows an old building, like a school or a hospital, perhaps.<br /> <br /> [what really is the case:]<br /> The Awakened of the city angered [insert cataclysmically powerful being] and brought a curse on themselves. The mage in question was a Mastigos Master of the third degree who found a secret weakness of the enemy, but unable to fight him, and unable to escape the curse, he hid the knowledge inside the mind of a Jamal Brown, who went catatonic from the experience, and was placed in the Lady of Compassion Mental Institution (in the picture).<br /> If the PCs can project into the Astral while in Jamal's presence, they'll enter his mind, which is a magical realm where they can uncover the secret and also try to save Jamal from his trauma.<br /> Insert various clues about this, Jamal can be scryed upon, is in the list of patients of the mental hospital etc. Also, the Astral version of Jamal's mind is a magical chaotic place, go nuts with it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (this is based on the initial plot hook of my previous Mage campaign)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1566-orabilis","name":"Orabilis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1566_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-18T17:12:27-08:00","id":1432641,"title":"","content":"A shaken member of the local Free Council (or whatever) shows up to a meeting. Apparently, he just figured out that whenever his uncle Larry does the &quot;pull my finger&quot; gag, there's a quake or volcanic eruption somewhere on the planet. Thousands have died from the effects of these bizarre coincident events, so he's trying to figure out what's possibly going on. He's also started trying to convince his uncle to quit doing it until he can suss it out, but both efforts have been going similarly poorly; Uncle Larry is set in his ways and telling him the discovery really won't help convince the irascible old fart to stop.<br /> <br /> He's checked spells and ghosts, and is pretty confident the secret doesn't lie in those, but needs a hand checking other esoteria. So far, the only pattern he's found is that the scale of the toot and the power of the natural(?) event correlate. Location may have a pattern, but as yet undiscovered, if so.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-23T21:08:58-08:00","id":1433215,"title":"","content":"<b>193)</b> We were exploring a Temenos realm of sci-fi, you know, taking a break by assuming roles in classic movies. We were in the Alien movie. One of our cabal members brought their familiar in via an entrance in the Shadow of a movie studio. It got infected by a chestburster and it...incorporated its Essence into its own, gaining its Manifestations and tenacious hunger. <br /> <br /> We tried to quarantine the realm, but it has been reproducing while following the trail of predatory realms to the Shadow exit. One recently broke through, the rest of the hive is soon to follow. We need to prepare ourselves, they are coming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-24-2021, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T08:26:35-08:00","id":1439179,"title":"","content":"<b>194)</b> Rumors are going around of &quot;Books of Magic&quot; that grant the power to cast spells to those who read and master them. Standard Sleeper nonsense. Except this time is holds a disturbing degree of truth - Sleepers who read these books <i>do</i> gain some knowledge of the Arcana, though they possess no Gnosis, Path, nor Wisdom. They do have Awakened-like Obsessions, though - to locate more of the books and grow their knowledge. Each one seems tied to one of the Arcana, and each one these former-Sleepers read grants greater mastery, unbound by the limits of their non-existent Gnosis. Though they hold recognizable Truths to Awakened eyes, they yield no special effect upon them. What is going on?<br /> <br /> <b>A)</b> Upon detailed examination, you have uncovered Symbols of Tyranny in these books. A plot by the Exarchs to replace the Seers with more culpable minions?<br /> <br /> <b>B)</b> These false-Mages have one notable characteristic - they still seem to count as Sleepers for the purposes of exaggerating Paradox. Even for their own spells. Without Wisdom to contain it, Intrusions are cropping up in greater number.<br /> <br /> <b>C)</b> These books are only appearing in the local area, and efforts to remove them cause them to vanish. Likewise, these false-Mages only retain their Arcana (and memories of their powers) so long as they remain in the region. It is obviously a localized phenomena, but what caused it, why, and how can this be used?<br /> <br /> <b>D)</b> <i>You</i> are one of these people who have learned True Magic, and these other people are looking at you like some oddity. Even talking about removing you and those like you as a threat. Can you escape these &quot;Awakened&quot; before they put their plans into action?<br /> <br /> [For running such characters, just give them few dots in Arcana, and let them use Resolve + Composure in place of Gnosis for most purposes, like Mana Capacity, spell casting Dice Pool, Yantras, and Combined Spells. They have no limits on Arcana ratings, but can't increase them on their own. All Arcana are treated as In Path (no +1 Mana cost for casting), and they can use Mana to mitigate Paradox, but don't have Wisdom to Contain it.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T16:41:30-07:00","id":1457156,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>195)</b> Consilium's emergency money is lost during the last night</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>196) </b>Dictionaries' pages in Mysterium's Atheneum are appearing in supernal scribe<br /> <b>197)</b> G</span><span style=\"font-family:arial\">uard spirits in Silver Ladder HQ are rising/lowering on their Ranks</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>198)</b> <i>(can be the second arc for previous plot hook)</i> Spirt Courts are kidnapping Thyrsi mages</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>199)</b> <i>(can be the third arc for <b>197</b> plot hook)</i> Obrimos from Adamantine Arrow woke up one day and now is a Master of Spirit, even having his own Spirit Court</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>200)</b> Oaths in Adamantine Arrow are twisting themselves and cursing their oahtkeepers</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>201) </b>Free Council spies are betraying their Order and giving intel to the Seers</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>202)</b> Guardian of the Veil's Masks are getting life on their own, having a body, mind and soul, trying to kill their former owners</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>203)</b> Players exchange bodies with local seer's cabal. Seers also don't know why this happened. Bonus: The players are in possession of their Prelacies and are hearing the Exarchs voices and receiving their omens</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>204)</b> Local Apostastes are reuniting themselves in a underground music show</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>205)</b> Proximii dystany from The Mysterium are all Awakening, but not the their parent Path</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>206)</b> Sleepwalker son of the Hierarch is offering his hand in marriage to anyone (no matter gender he's bi anyway) that brings him an artifact he dreamt of last night</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>207)</b> Filthy rich mage from Silver Ladder lost himself in Astral Realm and is trying to warn mages about &quot;That Which Devours Richies&quot; astral creature</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>208)</b> Emissary from Free Council ressurected from the dead after comitting suicide due to soul loss by the Tremere</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>209)</b> All people who Awake from the result of experiments from Awakening Gambit Legacy mages are now getting back to be Sleepers. The only one who remained a mage was a teenage girl from Guardians of the Veil</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>210)</b> Someone close to one of the players Awakes and even not being a Seer, that person is displaying signs of having a Prelacy</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>211)</b> Apostate mages are soon opening an auction to sell Soulstones. These soulstones are from living mages (players included), but the players (nor other mages) remember to do soulstones of themselvesand they aren't feeling part of their soul was taken off (because it wasn't)<br /> <b>212)</b> Precious stones and metals (diamonds, gold, etc) are losing their monetary value in an abnormal speed, making all Moroii being able to use lower levels of Matter to convert stuff to these now cheap materials</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>213)</b> All Mastigoi are losing connection with their daimons</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>214)</b> Animals and spirits are getting aggressive towards Thyris mages, to the point many died by animal and spirit brute violence</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>215)</b> Obrimoi mages are losing their passion on things, making them losing touch with Prime, but getting attuned with Death</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>216)</b> Dreams of prophecies are running wild in all Acanthi's minds during night, making them having a hivemind-like connection in Astral Realm<br /> <b>217)</b> The percentage of Pathless mages (sourcebook: Mage Chronicler's Guide) Awakening is getting higher and higher each day</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>218)</b> The Watchtower of Brass and Flame (sourcebook: Mage Chronicler's Guide) is estabilished as the 6th Watchtower in Atlantean canon. The Diamond is now accepting the mages from this Watchtower with open arms. The thing is: These mages are dreaming with another version of Atlantis and not the one The Diamond loves to talk about</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>219)</b> Local cabal of Banishers is assaulting sanctuns all over the town, but they are not robbing anything nor hurting anyone</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>220)</b> Sleepers are getting kidnapped to the far end of Astral Realms during dreams and are coming back next day with artifacts in their hands</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>212)</b> Cats all over the town are visiting sanctuns and leaving dead animals on its doors</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>213)</b> New taffy candy brand arrives in town and mages who eat it are having their mana pool recharged</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>214)</b> Supernal verges are more frequent each day</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>215)</b> FedEx is delivering ancient tomes filled with supernal scribes to mages with Wisdom 8+</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>216)</b> Mages' grandmas and grandpas are starting to saying &quot;in my times, mages like you didn't go around doing magic like that and risking getting caught by Paradox!&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2511-broskandar","name":"Broskandar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T12:56:08-07:00","id":1462919,"title":"","content":"<b>217/)The House That Isn\u2019t</b><br /> A powerful Arcadian Verge has been discovered in a small Midwest American town, an old Estate from the 1880s. The owner, who made it into Ripley\u2019s Believe It or Not as the oldest man in his state, recently died.<br /> <br /> He left no heirs, and no one was aware as to whether the old man was Awakened. Furthermore, no faction has laid claim to the Verge, so, the Consilium sends the PCs to snag the house for the Pentacle.<br /> <br /> Upon entering the house and peering into Twilight, the rickety old building turns into a labyrinth of rooms and hallways and additional levels, all festooned with ephemeral clocks. The doors in Twilight are all locked, and terrible noises can be heard from the other side of the doors. The Twilight side of the house\u2019s basement is flooded, and alien things Swim the waters.<br /> <br /> The house isn\u2019t empty. A strange spirit of the Shadow Realm, the Clockman, has taken up residence here. The Arcadian Mana has warped the spirit, disbarred b it from the flow of linear time. Killing it is next to impossible, as it\u2019s learnt to jump into parallel timelines! It intends to draw the material side of the house into a Place-That-Isn\u2019t an Emanation Realm of confusion, time and contradiction.<br /> <br /> Can the Cabal salvage the situation, or will the situation explode out of control?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-12T01:54:29-08:00","id":1472297,"title":"","content":"<br /> 218) <b>Supernatural malice makes Pandemic worse</b><br /> <br /> Thanks to the heroic efforts of the Assembly/Consilium to use their influence to get people to take the proper steps to help slow the spread of the pandemic, and the Seers of the Thrones ceasing assaults on cabals not resisting Panopticon and Hegemony use of their tyrannical authority, propaganda and underhanded coercion to take advantage of the environment of fear and general outcry for safety and stability while draconically enforcing &quot;safety theatre&quot; steps which reassure their frightened sleeper, the spread of the pandemic locally had almost stopped. Everyone was still following the steps to slow down the spread, working it into their everyday lives as &quot;the new normal&quot;...<br /> <br /> <u>Which is when <i><b>IT</b></i> happened!! </u><br /> <br /> Suddenly hospital after hospital had their staff and patients catch the disease of the pandemic at the same time. The sleepers are insane with fear, and even the mage community is in an uproar. The PCs react as they do during these events.<br /> <br /> If the PCs don't get involved another way then a young Thyrsus ally of the PC's cabal. whom was set up in advance a few stories before this one seeks their help. The ally was healing a loved one at the hospital and noticed<i> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=809977#post809977\">something</a> </i>using preternatural means to remain unseen that set off his mage sight. It wasn't a spirit, a living being, nor a restless dead. By process of elimination and word of caution spoken by his mentor he believes it must be an Abyssal Intruder, which frightens him to his core. He has come for emotional backup and advice before bringing this to the attention of the Assembly/Consilium.<br /> <br /> He describes what he saw with mage sight as a foul miasma stinking of corpse rot with dried flower petals drifting through it in a roughly humanoid shape with and everchanging ceramic mask dripping putrid fluid with each step, but that's just a symbolic representation, and he never actually saw it.<br /> <br /> The &quot;something&quot;...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=809977#post809977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Plague Walker</b></span><br /> The earliest account of the creature known as \u201cPlague Walker\u201d is a description and woodcut in a book called \u201cMaledetta Anno \u201c, written by Italian monks in 1350, during the years of the Black Death. Since that time it appears in places suffering the outbreak of an illness, invisible to all except the infected. It has worn many faces over the ages, but always dressed in pure white robes, has red eyes and limbs covered in weeping sores. It carries scent like potpourri covering the smell of death. Its current face is that of a young, fair-skinned woman with dark hair. The creature seems to avoid those with cancer or genetic conditions, and limits its depredations to contagions.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Compassion; <b>Vice: </b>Dutiful<br /> <b>Aspiration: </b>Spread Disease<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 7, Wits 6, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 8, Stamina 6<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 4, Composure 6<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 3, Empathy 6(Suffering), Brawl 3(Touch), Intimidate 4, Medicine 6(Contagion), Occult 4, Science 4, Stealth 6, Subterfuge 6<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area of Expertise (Contagion), Defensive Combat (Brawl), Encyclopedic Knowledge (Outbreaks), Fighting Finesse (Touch), Holistic Awareness, Hardy 3, Iron Will, Style: Unarmed Defense 3<br /> <b>Potency: </b>7<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 18<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 14<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 9<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 18; Flight 28<br /> <b>Health:</b> 11<br /> <b>Ban:</b> cannot approach a person wearing a garland of roses or garlic<br /> <b>Bane:</b> sterilized implements<br /> <b>Dread Powers: </b>Immortality, Influence (Contagions) 3, <b><i>Invisibility*</i></b><br /> <br /> <b><i><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Invisibility: </span></i></b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The horror does not register to sight, often times even under infrared or ultraviolet light. Perception rolls to spot the creature suffer a \u20135 die penalty and unless they have a way of compensating for or negating the invisibility, attackers are considered to be fighting blind. In most cases Invisibility is a permanent aspect of the creature, but some can control when they are visible. In the latter case, altering its visibility for a scene costs the Horror one point of Willpower. The creature\u2019s invisibility typically has a condition where it does not apply (such as infrared light, when observed by children or through electronic recording devices).</span><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-12-2022, 05:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T18:09:24-08:00","id":1474150,"title":"","content":"<b>219) </b>The battles had worn at him. The Seers, the Abyss, the Banishers, yet the veteran Arrow carried on. Ruthless, but efficient, a brilliant inventor, the one you called when you needed to solve things then or face unimaginable consequences. Well, someone finally managed to kill him and we thought that was the end of it. If only things were so simple. In his paranoia, he made a backup of his mind, so he could always be consulted in case he fell.<br /> <br /> But he had more than one backup and he wasn't planning on allowing death to beat him. With great skill in Life and Mind magic, he transformed one of his backup goetias. The idea was made into an emotion, an infectious emotion. Enough people have been infected, the emotion has become Resonance and it has started to coalesce, causing his rebirth into a spirit human. We don't know if he will have any Awakened powers, we don't want to find out, the combination of a brutal mage with the madness of the Shadow must not become a reality. So that is the situation this cabal uncovered, its why you are all here, we now need to figure out out next moves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}